msgid "\"Keep the armor you already have; I will not issue another suit. If you agree, I will prepare an escape charm. The attack will begin only when you activate it here and confirm. Equip and pack first. Escape through the western road or southern garden, not through victory over both apostles.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "\"Questions and receiving armor do not commit you to battle. A separate readiness response prepares the charm, and its activation starts the attack. If you have not survived the Eclipse or are away from my manor, that preparation is unavailable.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "\"The escape has ended. Seek shelter and recover; your hunt journal can guide you to the remaining apostles. My gift remains yours, but the grove can no longer protect you.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "\"The sanctuary is lost, but your road continues. Recover, then follow the unfinished hunts. There will be no second attack on this house.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "\"You have confirmed readiness. The charm waits for your decision; there is no attack clock yet. Return here with your equipment and activate it when ready.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "*Flora turns to you and waits for you to speak."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Flora could not confirm readiness. Speak to her in the peaceful registered manor after surviving the Eclipse. You need either her armor gift or an existing complete or packed suit; an attack already begun cannot be prepared again."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Flora's sanctuary has fallen. The escape is complete and the attack cannot be restarted. Recover at your refuge, then activate your apostle hunt journal to choose an unfinished trail."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Flora's token for a one-time escape. First speak to her in her manor and explicitly confirm readiness; receiving or wearing armor alone is not enough. An existing complete or packed suit has its own readiness response. Equip and pack before activating this charm in the registered manor. A confirmation starts the attack: guardians delay Zodd and Grunbeld while you escape through the western road or southern garden. It needs no power, does not teleport you and cannot restart a completed attack."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "I already have the armor. Help me prepare for the attack."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "I understand. Confirm my readiness and give me the escape charm."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Let us speak."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Not now."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Readiness has not been confirmed. Speak to Flora and explicitly agree to prepare the attack. If you already have the armor, choose the armor-owner readiness response. Merely receiving or wearing armor is not enough."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Readiness is confirmed and Flora gives you an escape charm. Your existing armor is kept; missing pieces are entrusted only once. Equip and pack what you need, then activate the charm inside her manor. The attack waits for your explicit confirmation. Escape by the western road or southern garden; you need not kill the apostles."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Readiness is confirmed. Equip and pack what you need, then activate Flora's escape charm inside the registered manor. Until you confirm activation, the attack does not begin."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "Speak to Flora in her manor. You can ask questions and receive the missing armor without beginning an attack. Readiness requires a separate dialogue confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "The attack has already begun. Leave through the western road or southern garden and go beyond the grove; the charm cannot restart it."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "The attack on Flora's manor is underway. Leave by the western road or the southern garden, then go beyond the grove."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "The escape is already complete. Flora's manor has fallen; this charm cannot start the attack again."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "The charm remains silent. Speak with Flora here, beside the spiritual tree."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "The manor is not in its peaceful preparation state. Speak to Flora before trying again."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "What is the next step in our plan?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "You are outside the registered manor. Return to Flora's house or its southern gardens, then activate the charm when ready."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "You have already resolved the armor gift. To prepare the attack, speak to Flora and choose the separate readiness response for an armor owner. Receiving or wearing the armor does not confirm readiness."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "You must survive the Eclipse before preparing Flora's attack. The charm does nothing for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_eocs.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json items/flora_escape_charm.json
msgid "You postpone the attack. Readiness remains confirmed; activate the charm again when your preparations are complete."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "First hunt: the apostle's hollow"
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Find the apostle in the marked forest hollow and defeat it. Recover from the Eclipse and prepare a ward and your equipment before approaching. After victory, search its remains for a burned scrap and activate the scrap to trace a nearby breach. The mission does not require the Skull Knight to remain nearby."
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "first-hunt notes"
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "The Skull Knight's first trail after the Eclipse. Activate to recover the same hunt target or retry a failed search after travelling. Track the hollow through the missions menu; the notes never create a second lair after a target has been recorded. After victory, they remind you to collect and activate the burned scrap. No living guide or literacy is needed."
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Recall the first hunt"
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "First hunt added to your missions: the apostle's hollow. Its target is the marked forest hollow. Recover, prepare a ward and your equipment, then follow the mission marker. Search the apostle's remains for a burned scrap after the battle."
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Your saved hunt location could not be verified. It has been kept unchanged; no replacement lair or duplicate mission was created. Check the save and report this message."
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "No safe forest hollow was found 8-16 overmap tiles away. No hunt has been assigned. Search retries at most three times here; travel at least 24 local tiles and activate your first-hunt notes to try from another position. Explored terrain is never replaced."
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "The first hunt still points to the same hollow. Select \"First hunt: the apostle's hollow\" in your missions menu to track it on the overmap. Other hunts keep their own progress."
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "First hunt completed. Search the apostle's remains, take the burned scrap and activate it to locate the nearby breach. You do not need the Skull Knight to continue."
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Survive the Eclipse and return to the surface before following the first hunt."
msgstr ""

#: missions/first_hunt.json effects/first_hunt_eocs.json items/first_hunt_directions.json dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Remind me where the first hunt leads."
msgstr ""

#: effects/eclipse_grasp_eocs.json effects/eclipse_story_effects.json effects/eclipse_expanded_final_eocs.json
msgid "Watching in silence"
msgstr ""

#: effects/eclipse_grasp_eocs.json effects/eclipse_story_effects.json effects/eclipse_expanded_final_eocs.json
msgid "Griffith waits motionless for the confrontation."
msgstr ""

#: effects/eclipse_grasp_eocs.json effects/eclipse_story_effects.json effects/eclipse_expanded_final_eocs.json
msgid "The center of the ceremony is blocked. Griffith could not appear; no confrontation has started. Clear the center and leave and re-enter the ceremony to retry."
msgstr ""

#: effects/eclipse_grasp_eocs.json effects/eclipse_story_effects.json effects/eclipse_expanded_final_eocs.json
msgid "Griffith stands before you, silent and untouched by the slaughter. The sight of him drives you into a blind rage. Demons close in from every side and seize your left wrist. You hack through your own wrist to tear free; a claw destroys one eye as you wrench yourself out of their grip. Your left hand is gone and your Perception is halved. Close this window to resume the fight."
msgstr ""

#: effects/eclipse_grasp_eocs.json effects/eclipse_story_effects.json effects/eclipse_expanded_final_eocs.json
msgid "Griffith stands before you, silent and untouched by the slaughter. The sight of him drives you into a blind rage. Demons close in from every side and seize your left wrist. You hack through your own wrist to tear free as claws rake your scarred face. Your left hand is gone; your existing eye wound is not applied a second time. Close this window to resume the fight."
msgstr ""

#: effects/eclipse_grasp_eocs.json effects/eclipse_story_effects.json effects/eclipse_expanded_final_eocs.json
msgid "Griffith stands before you, silent and untouched by the slaughter. The sight of him drives you into a blind rage. Demons close in from every side. You wrench your already ruined left arm from their grip, but a claw destroys one eye. Your existing hand wound or arm cannon is preserved; your Perception is halved. Close this window to resume the fight."
msgstr ""

#: effects/eclipse_grasp_eocs.json effects/eclipse_story_effects.json effects/eclipse_expanded_final_eocs.json
msgid "Griffith stands before you, silent and untouched by the slaughter. The sight of him drives you into a blind rage. Demons close in from every side. You tear your already ruined arm free as claws rake your scarred face. Your existing wounds and any installed arm cannon are preserved. Close this window to resume the fight."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_arena_eocs.json furniture/hunt_arenas.json
msgid "Something stirs behind the cover inside the lair. The encounter has begun; retreat remains possible."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_arena_eocs.json furniture/hunt_arenas.json
msgid "This is an older lair without an encounter record. No second guardian has been created. Return while its original guardian is nearby; an absent old guardian must be checked before a replacement is allowed."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_arena_eocs.json furniture/hunt_arenas.json
msgid "Every arrival point is in view. Move behind cover inside the arena; the guardian will not appear in front of you."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_arena_eocs.json furniture/hunt_arenas.json
msgid "The hidden arrival points are blocked. No guardian was created. Clear a recess, then examine the battle-scarred ground inside the arena to retry."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_arena_eocs.json furniture/hunt_arenas.json
msgid "battle-scarred ground"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_arena_eocs.json furniture/hunt_arenas.json
msgid "Deep tracks cross the center of the lair. Its guardian emerges from cover when you enter this inner area. If its arrival was blocked, clear a recess and examine these tracks to retry."
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "A cord of bones hangs at the southwestern edge of the clearing. Examine it to wind a delayed mechanism: four bursts begin after 20 seconds, then repeat every 15 seconds. It can be wound again after 90 seconds. Hide behind solid cover before the first burst; noise will not make a creature ignore visible prey."
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "A weighted stone chime hangs in the western passage, away from the eastern relic chamber. Examine it to wind a delayed mechanism: four bursts begin after 20 seconds, then repeat every 15 seconds. It can be wound again after 90 seconds. Hide behind solid cover before the first burst; noise will not make a creature ignore visible prey."
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "The fallen bell hangs from a frame in the southern nave, far from the northern reliquary. Examine it to wind a delayed mechanism: four bursts begin after 20 seconds, then repeat every 15 seconds. It can be wound again after 90 seconds. Hide behind solid cover before the first burst; noise will not make a creature ignore visible prey."
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "A hand-cranked siren lies at the southwestern edge of the abandoned tent camp. Examine it to wind a delayed mechanism: four bursts begin after 20 seconds, then repeat every 15 seconds. It can be wound again after 90 seconds. Hide behind solid cover before the first burst; noise will not make a creature ignore visible prey."
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "You wind the mechanism. The first noise will come from this device in 20 seconds; get behind cover. Four bursts will follow, then it will stop."
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "The delayed mechanism is wound. It will make four bursts of noise, then stop. It cannot be wound again until 90 seconds after activation."
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "This mechanism is already wound. It will stop by itself and can be wound again 90 seconds after activation."
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "The inscription reads: \"We hid the red stone in the northern reliquary. Wind the bell, hide, and wait for its delayed peals. The thing follows sounds when it has lost sight of prey. Circle through the broken west wall while it searches the nave.\""
msgstr ""

#: effects/behelit_site_eocs.json effects/behelit_distraction_eocs.json furniture/behelit_sites.json furniture/behelit_distractions.json
msgid "The final entry reads: \"Specimen: a red stone face, secured in the northeastern tent. A human-shaped predator keeps returning to it. Wind the siren, hide behind the tents before it starts, then approach the case from the other side. Noise cannot distract a creature that still sees you.\""
msgstr ""

#: effects/grunbeld_breath_eocs.json effects/grunbeld_combat_effects.json spells/grunbeld_breath.json fields/grunbeld_breath.json monsters/apostle_grunbeld.json monster_special_attacks/grunbeld_attacks.json
