#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "A roar breaks the silence. The guardian emerges into the arena. Prepare to fight or retreat."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Adds content inspired by Kentaro Miura's Berserk. Face beings tied to the God Hand, battle legendary demons, or forge and wield Guts' legendary sword. Intended for a prepared mid-game survivor: its demons and apostles are dangerous for a fresh character. Bring armor, medical supplies and an escape plan before pursuing the story."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Eclipse rescue recovery"
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Restore stamina once after the Skull Knight brings you back."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Rosine folds her wings for a dive! Leave the marked line now: she dives in one second!"
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Show the first hunt on my map."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "The first hunt is complete. Read the directions you recovered and inspect the marked ashen breach. You can also ask me for the path to Flora."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "The first hunt leads to a forest hollow held by a lesser apostle. Select the first hunt in your mission journal to see its target. Prepare armor, medical supplies and a way to retreat before entering the hollow."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "apostle hunt journal"
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Trails to the Count, Wyald, Rosine and Grunbeld. Activate to review the trails one at a time: Yes selects the displayed trail; No continues to the next. Grunbeld opens after the other three breaches are sealed. Each hunt keeps its own progress and one-time reward."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Trace the Count's residence? Yes selects this trail. No shows the next trail or the hunt summary."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Trace Wyald and the Black Dogs? Yes selects this trail. No shows the next trail or the hunt summary."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Trace Rosine's Mistvale? Yes selects this trail. No shows the next trail or the hunt summary."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-01
msgid "Trace Grunbeld's scarred stronghold? Yes selects this trail. No shows the next trail or the hunt summary."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-02
msgid "Where can I find Flora before the next apostle hunt?"
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-02
msgid "\"Visit Flora before hunting the named apostles. She can give you the missing armor pieces and explain their price; you need not defeat the Count, Wyald or Rosine first. I have given you directions to her forest manor. Activate them to recover the route if the search fails. If you own the whole suit, ask her for counsel and preparation instead.\""
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-02
msgid "You already own the armor or accepted Flora's gift. In her peaceful manor, choose the separate readiness response when you are prepared. Wearing armor alone does not begin an attack."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-02
msgid "You are speaking to Flora. Choose \"Will you entrust the armor to me?\" to receive missing pieces. The gift does not start an attack. Preparing the escape separately requires her peaceful manor."
msgstr ""

#: playtest-fixes-2026-10-02
msgid "After completing the first hunt, ask the Skull Knight for Flora's directions or activate those directions. Visit her before the named apostle hunts to ask about the armor. A complete or packed suit does not need a second gift."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "broken root-cutter"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A hand-forged blade with a split wooden haft. Dark sap fills the break. Activate it to examine the marks left by its owner."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Fresh cuts stop halfway through the roots. Two sets of tally marks were scratched into the haft; one ends abruptly. They meant to cut a path to the stone face, not to fight what lived beneath it."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "wayfarer's tied ward"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A cloth knot and a small carved bone, carefully tied around a cord. This personal keepsake grants no protection. Activate it to examine the inscription."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "The inscription names two travelers and asks that both return home. A second knot was added with a shaking hand. Beyond it, the bark bears the same dark stain as the abandoned cutting tool."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "oak traveler's last note"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A handwritten scrap protected inside folded cloth. Activate it to read the last account of a search beneath the oak."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "We left the cart on the old track. The stone face is in the roots, just as he said. The bones ring at the far edge; the roots turn toward them. If I reach the center, I will come back by the eastern gap. If only one of us returns, leave the other name on the cord."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Only scraps of the old wrapping remain."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Nothing could be recovered here."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "You lay the recovered belongings here. Pick them up before leaving."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Collect the abandoned belongings?"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "abandoned cart bundle"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A road bundle lies among split wooden wheels. A broken root-cutting tool protrudes from the cloth."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "cold campfire bundle"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Cold ashes surround a small cloth bundle. A handwritten scrap is tucked inside."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "ward tied to a root"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A carved bone and two cloth knots were tied to this root by someone who hoped to return."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "abandoned cloth provision bundle"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A cloth bundle holding a few old-fashioned provisions. It contains no modern equipment."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "searched bundle"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "The wrapping has been opened and the contents removed."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "ancient oak trunk"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A massive section of the old oak. Its twisted trunk forms a solid screen around the root pocket."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "knotted oak roots"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Thick roots rise into a barrier. Gaps between the clusters lead around the center."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Leader of the Black Dogs, swollen into a hulking apostle. He braces before a charge along a fixed line. Cover or a sidestep can break the rush. The collision of worlds diverted his former fate: this is the living Wyald, not a projection. Defeating him exposes the camp's breach."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Griffith's Eclipse manifestation"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A manifestation of Griffith at the ritual heart of the Eclipse. The God Hand are not ordinary apostles. Breaking this form disrupts the local scene; it does not kill the being beyond it."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "'You shattered the manifestation. Do not mistake that for killing one of the God Hand. This place is breaking around us; come with me while the way is open.'"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "'The Behelit opened a place of sacrifice along the boundary where our worlds collided. Your Eclipse widened those wounds; it did not create this world's first catastrophe. I could not undo the sacrifice. I cut a way out while someone remained to save.'"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Why are beings from another world still alive here?"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "'The collision broke more than the ground. Some lives were drawn away from the deaths that awaited them. Wyald survived his former fate and came here with the Black Dogs. That does not make every apostle a projection. Kill a living original and that life ends; breaking a reflection leaves its source untouched.'"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "How did the two worlds collide?"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "\"I am a witch, not a fairy, and this house stands beside a spiritual tree. The first collision joined wounds in your world to paths in ours. Your Eclipse deepened those openings, drawing more creatures across. Quieting one breach helps the land nearby; it cannot mend every wound or erase your Brand.\""
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Flora's herbal folio"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "A handwritten folio with pressed leaves, small household sketches and corrections in the margins. Activate it to read."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Dry the herbs separately. Boil clean cloth for wounds. Mend the old sleeves before another journey. Keep both paths around the spiritual tree clear. The last line reads: a refuge remains a refuge because someone cares for it."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "The old track ends at broken cart wheels. Thick roots surround the stone face; a gap on the eastern side offers a second way around. A cold camp and a tied ward mark where two travelers stopped."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "old cart tracks"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "Deep wheel marks stop beside splintered wooden wheels. A cloth bundle rests nearby."
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "bare cord on a root"
msgstr ""

#. Location content foundation, October 2026
msgid "The personal ward has been untied. Only its fastening cord remains."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "cave scout's route sketch"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A hand-drawn route on folded cloth. Activate it to read the marks."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The broad gallery bends east, then south toward the hollow. The cramped passage turns southwest around the stone mass. Crouch and keep behind the bends; the listener hunts by sight as well as sound. The stone chime is in a side chamber. A wooden brace can be released from the far side to shorten the return to the ladder."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "chapel relief roster"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Names, meal portions and blanket assignments fill these pages. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "First week: water and dressings in the south pantry, books in the sacristy, graves outside the west wall. Later entries replace the meal counts with hours spent beside the red stone. The last volunteer underlined: this was meant to be a shelter."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "reliquary keeper's confession"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Black wax stains the margin of a prayer sheet. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "We called the stone a miracle because we needed one. We moved it behind the altar and stopped opening the door to strangers. When the bell rang by itself, we thought we had been answered. The handprints on the altar were not made in prayer."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "refugee's forest directions"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A folded note describes another place where a red face was seen. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "If the chapel is lost, leave through the broken west wall. An old cart track farther into the forest ends at a huge oak with knotted roots. Travelers spoke of another stone face there. This is a lead, not a surveyed map; do not mistake the tree for safety."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "expedition transport order"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A transport checklist lists the specimen, missing sleep and a cancelled departure. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Departure was delayed to repeat the measurements. The siren was moved southwest so nobody would have to stand beside the specimen to test it. We kept the case in camp because the nightmares followed it. That was our mistake: we treated a warning as a reason to stay."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "abandoned leather scout pack"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A worn leather pack rests in the entrance pocket, above the wet stone. Its owner drew a route before descending farther."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "empty lamp tied to a rope"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A clay lamp hangs from a rope beside the return passage. Its wick is dry; examine it to recover the lamp and cord."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "chapel relief cabinet"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Dressings and a list of sheltered people remain in this south-side cabinet."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "chapel food cupboard"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The congregation stored drinking water, food and an escape note here before the rituals began."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "expedition medical crate"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Field medicines remain beside the sleeping place of the expedition medic."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "expedition repair crate"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A finite stock of tools, spare batteries and a district road map survived under the torn tent."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "claw-scored cave stone"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Deep scratches cross an old hand-cut arrow. Examine the stone."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The first scratches point inward; later marks point back. Something dragged a burden through the broad gallery. A strip of cloth was tied behind the turn, where the ladder can no longer be seen."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "layered return marks"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Several travelers scratched different exit arrows into the rock."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Three attempts are visible: chalk, knife cuts, then fingernails. The narrow route still joins the gallery at the far end. The fresh wooden brace belongs to a return shortcut; its fastening is on the inner side. This cave is not named in the notes."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "specimen measurement board"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "String, marks and an unfinished diagram remain beside the sample tent."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Measurements moved farther from the case every day, but the same names appear in the sleep log. The team's last diagram shows the siren to the southwest and a clear route around the northern tent. Testing the alarm from cover would have been safer than standing beside the specimen."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "braced cave passage"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A fallen slab is held across the narrow passage by a wooden brace. The release is farther inside the cave."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "inner cave brace release"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A wooden peg holds the shortcut shut. Examine it from this inner passage to clear the way back."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "released cave brace fastening"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The return passage has been cleared."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "You release the brace. The slab settles aside and the short route to the entrance is open."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "expedition canvas groundsheet"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A stretched waterproof groundsheet covers the soil inside the tent. Furniture and belongings rest on it."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "loose cave scree"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "Loose fragments cover the broad gallery. The uneven footing slows movement; crouch around the bends and keep out of the keeper's sight."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A Behelit rests in the far eastern stone hollow. Examine it when the keeper is away."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "A weighted stone chime hangs in a western acoustic side chamber, away from the relic. Wind it, then retreat behind the bends before its first burst in 20 seconds. Four bursts repeat every 15 seconds; it resets after 90 seconds. Noise does not make the guardian forget visible prey."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The cracked bell stands in the western ground-floor bell room. Wind it, hide before the first peal in 20 seconds, and use the sacristy or broken west wall to circle north. Four bursts repeat every 15 seconds; it resets after 90 seconds. Visible prey remains a target."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The leader's tent is northwest, the specimen northeast, medical supplies southwest and the torn store southeast. The rope cordon is broken on the eastern side. Nobody finished packing; the transport order explains why they stayed."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The chapel first sheltered strangers. Meal lists remain in the southern aid cupboard; black wax and handprints cover the northern altar. The sacristy joins the broken west wall. The bell room is southwest, away from the relic."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The inscription reads: \"The red stone is behind the northern altar. The southwest bell room and the broken west wall offer another approach. Read the aid roster before you follow the prayers: this place changed after the stone arrived.\""
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The final entry reads: \"We could not sleep, so we delayed leaving to measure the stone again. The case is in the northeast tent. The repair crate has a district map; the siren is southwest. Wind it from cover and circle behind the tents. We should have left before the dreams began.\""
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "scout pack resting place"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The pack and its belongings have been recovered. Only their outline remains on the dry stone."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "bare lamp fastening"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The empty lamp and rope are gone. A small knot remains caught in the rock."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "empty relief cabinet"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The aid cabinet has been searched; the remaining supplies are gone."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "empty chapel food cupboard"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The food cupboard has been searched. The congregation left nothing else here."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "searched medical crate"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The finite medical stock has been recovered. Only dividers remain in the crate."
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "searched repair crate"
msgstr ""

#. Cave, chapel and expedition detail, October 2026
msgid "The tools, spare batteries and map have been recovered. The crate holds no further supplies."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "bruised living ground"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Broad purple scars cross the yielding surface."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "exposed sinews"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Bundles of pale sinews run toward the ceremony like stretched cords."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "wall of enormous faces"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Closed eyes and mouths merge into a vast, impassable boundary."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "entwined bodies"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Interlocked bodies rise beyond the field. There is no path through them."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "distant God Hand silhouette"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "An immense, silent presence watches the ceremony beyond the reach of any weapon. This is no ordinary apostle."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "swelling luminous vein"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A slow pulse lights the surrounding flesh, then recedes."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Wet tearing sounds come from behind the fold. Approaching the victims may draw the feeders out."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "blood-soaked feeding hollow"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "abandoned feeding tracks"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "The creature has already left this hollow. Nothing else waits here."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A feeder abandons the dead and claws its way around the flesh fold!"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A lone hunter circles beyond the fold. The wide path bypasses its tracks."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "fresh tracks into a fold"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "The lone hunter leaves its hollow. You hear its claws following the side trail."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "taut flesh diaphragm"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A thin sheet closes the short passage. Its loose edge can be pulled aside from the adjacent scar."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "loose edge of the diaphragm"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Pull the loose tissue aside to connect this branch to the main trail."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "opened flesh passage"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "The diaphragm has been pulled aside. This shortcut stays open."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Pull the diaphragm aside? This takes five seconds."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "The tissue parts. A short passage joins the scarred ground beyond."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "great luminous artery"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A slow heartbeat rises through this exposed artery. The nearby light swells and fades."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Beyond this scar Griffith waits. Coming within his reach begins an irreversible confrontation: you may lose your left hand and an eye. Finish any exploration and prepare before approaching him."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "last scar before the ceremony"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "The ash trail ends at the silent center. Approach only when ready for the final confrontation."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "crossed ceremony scar"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "The final gathering lies beyond this scar."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Confront Griffith now? You will be seized, lose any remaining left hand and one eye, and face the final battle. No route back opens until the scene ends."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Corkus's scabbard fragment"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A cracked piece of scabbard, polished where a hand held it too tightly. Carry it when speaking to the Skull Knight."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Gaston's sewing roll"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A crushed roll of needles and cloth, kept for a quieter life that never began. Carry it when speaking to the Skull Knight."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "last stand scratched on cloth"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A blood-stiffened scrap records an attempted retreat. Activate it to read the marks."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Three empty knife sheaths lie beside Judeau. His last throws bought someone a few breaths. Beyond him, the ash trail bends south between the pale sinews; the eastern branch leads to an abandoned satchel."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Pippin lies across the narrowest gap in the ridge. Scrapes on his hammer show where he held back the first rush. You can continue south along the western scars or rejoin the ash trail to the east."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "A fragment of scabbard is clenched beside Corkus. Something that looked like an escape drew him into the feast. The outer eastern flank remains open: you need not approach the feeding hollows."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Gaston's sewing roll has spilled beneath the battered breastplate. Beyond him, the enormous ribs lean toward a still, luminous center. Follow their curve south to the last ceremony scar."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "The torn satchel holds bread, dried meat, a waterskin and a few cloth dressings. Claws scrape behind a nearby fold. These supplies are finite; the main ash trail bypasses this exposed branch."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Fresh tracks vanish behind the northern fold. Approaching them may loose a single hunter; the broad western path skirts the hollow and reaches the last stand farther south."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Wet tearing sounds come from the screened feeding hollows. The creatures will leave the dead if you approach closely. An open path along the eastern edge skirts both the feast and the victims."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "The ash trail bends east toward the luminous ribs. Griffith waits beyond the final scar. Approaching him begins an irreversible scene; finish exploring and prepare before entering his reach."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "We kept the pale trail in sight. The left passage still held; the center had closed. If anyone follows, do not chase the light in the feeding pits. The great ribs bend toward the gathering."
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Corkus clutched this scabbard. Was there ever a way out?"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "'The ceremony used hope as another snare. Remember him as a man who wanted to live, not merely as another body in the feast.'"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Gaston kept this sewing roll. What became of his hopes?"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "'He carried the tools of a life beyond war. Taking them out of this darkness does not mend what was lost, but it denies the feast the last word.'"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "'You broke the manifestation that held this ceremony together. Do not mistake that for killing one of the God Hand. The wound is closing: come with me, now.'"
msgstr ""

#: eclipse-field-detail-2026-10-02
msgid "Griffith's manifestation breaks apart. The distant figures remain untouched. The ceremony shudders, and the Skull Knight cuts through its closing darkness."
msgstr ""

# Introductory hollow and ashen breach, October 2026

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "trampled hollow soil"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Loose earth and old drag marks fill a shallow depression behind the stones."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "ash-stained verge"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Ash has settled over an old track. Footprints end where the ground began to split."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "living fissure"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The ground splits into a wet, moving crack. Use the firm islands or the passage behind the broken walls."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "cooled breach scar"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The former wound has hardened into a firm, dark seam. It can be crossed."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "tucked-away survivor bundle"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "A fur blanket and a few belongings were hidden under the roots, away from the drag marks."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "searched belongings"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Only torn wrapping and marks in the earth remain."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "predator's gathered belongings"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The apostle piled the useful belongings of its prey here. Defeat it before searching this exposed stash."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The predator still holds this exposed patch. Defeat the apostle, then recover what its victims left."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "failed defenders' supply chest"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Dressings and water remain behind a broken wall. These people tried to hold the old post."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "gouged stone at the hollow edge"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Hooked scratches stop short of a root-covered retreat. Examine them before entering the depression."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Its lunges cross only a short gap. The wounded prey escaped by widening the distance; the apostle could not restore its torn flesh. Clear the two scavengers, keep the return track open, and draw it around the stone screens. You need preparation, not Flora's armor or perfect health."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "belongings of different travelers"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "A patched shirt, broken clasp and child-sized cord lie far from their owners."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The belongings do not match: a carter's knot, a traveler's patched shirt, a little cord tied as a charm. This predator took people one by one, not as part of a ceremony. Drag marks lead from the ruined stopping place into the hollow."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "broken line of ward stakes"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Snapped stakes and ash mark an attempt to contain the wound."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The old road ran past a small watch post. Someone ringed the crack with stakes and cloth wards; the ground tore through the foundations instead. Three firm patches remain. The open middle is short, while the western remains of the wall provide a covered approach."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "trampled ash beneath the prey"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The predator's tracks have churned the ash beyond recognition."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "revealed ashen trail"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "After the predator's fall, a scorched route can be traced among the prey's belongings."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The living predator leaves you no time to sort these tracks. Clear the hollow first."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The burned scrap carried by the apostle matches the ashen route here. Search its remains and activate the scrap to locate the separate breach. The gathered belongings can now be recovered."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "fallen post beam"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "A collapsed timber blocks a sheltered gap. Move it from the adjacent loose end."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "loose end of the beam"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The damaged timber can be shifted without a special tool."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "cleared covered gap"
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The collapsed beam has been shifted. This sheltered passage remains open."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Shift the loose beam to open the covered gap? This takes five seconds."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The beam slides aside. You can reach the seal behind the broken wall."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The pulse breaks with a dry crack, then falls silent."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "A slow, hollow heartbeat rises from the split ground."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The breach is sealed. Its influence has weakened for roughly two overmap tiles around this place. Demons that have already crossed remain nearby. The Brand has not vanished."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The first breach has not yet been recorded as sealed. Defeat its guardian, then examine the wound."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "This breach cannot be sealed yet: its guardian must be defeated, this must be your recorded first breach, and you must examine the open wound beside you. A sealed breach grants nothing again."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Show the region quieted by the first sealed breach? No continues to the next-path choices."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The moving crack cools into firm dark stone, and its heartbeat stops. New incursions are suppressed around this recorded breach, roughly two overmap tiles away; existing demons and your Brand remain. The journal can show this region again, then let you choose the next trail. Other apostles' breaches are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Records the first sealed breach and its locally quieted region. Activate to show that area without changing your chosen path, then consider Flora, a refuge or the Count's residence. Other hunts and breaches keep their own records; the Brand remains."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The ruined stop belonged to several travelers. Drag marks enter the hollow behind the stone folds; a root-covered shelter lies to the west. Examine the gouged stone before entering. Clear the scavengers or leave the perimeter route open for retreat."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "The road post split along its foundations. The short middle route crosses firm landings; the longer western route follows the remaining wall. The loose beam can open another covered gap. Defeat the keeper, then examine the wound: only this recorded region will quiet."
msgstr ""

#: effects/hunt_site_detail_eocs.json furniture/hunt_site_details.json
msgid "Find the apostle in the marked hollow. Inspect the ruined stop and the claw marks, recover the hidden supplies, then defeat the predator. You need prepared equipment, not full health or Flora's armor. Search its remains for the burned scrap and activate it to locate a separate breach. The Skull Knight need not remain nearby."
msgstr ""

# Refuge and Count residence detail, October 2026

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Within eight local tiles on this level, a bone and stone ward suppresses the Brand's extra nighttime summons, including on the ward's own tile. It does not stop roaming demons, armor-created shadows, zombies or attacks, and does not erase the Brand. Choose an existing defensible building; put your sleeping place inside the ward's reach, prepare light and drinking water, and keep an escape route. The ward needs no fuel or repeated servicing. You can record your own readiness here; light, water and bedding are a checklist, not an automatic safety guarantee."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "A bone and stone ward against the Brand's nighttime summons within eight local tiles on the same level. Examine it to review its limits and record a prepared refuge. It does not repel existing enemies, zombies or the armor's shadows, and needs no regular servicing."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Record this ward as your prepared refuge? Confirm only after arranging drinking water, light, a sleeping place within eight tiles and an escape route. This records your assessment; it does not build or inspect those supplies for you."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Refuge recorded. Stay within this ward's reach for the Brand's protection; keep watch for creatures that are already here. The refuge journal keeps your preparations and onward directions. It grants no healing, armor or immunity."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The ward works outdoors too, but this is not a sheltered sleeping place. Inspect it from inside a nearby building to record a refuge. Do not confuse its limited protection with walls and a roof."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Your chosen refuge is recorded at the ward's location. This is your readiness checklist, not a guarantee about its current walls, light or supplies."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "No prepared refuge is currently recorded. Inspect a ward from a sheltered adjacent tile and confirm your preparations."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The journal records a dawn reached after at least an hour of nighttime presence within the recorded ward's reach. This does not certify that no enemy could enter. You can rest or prepare your prosthesis before following a trail."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Read the next story direction? This does not require you to finish a night here or build a new base."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Dawn reaches the refuge. Your journal records the night watch by the ward. The Brand remains; recover here if you can, prepare the prosthesis, then consult your next trail."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The recorded ward is gone. Its journal entry no longer marks the refuge as ready; inspect another ward when your preparations are complete."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "refuge preparation journal"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Your chosen ward, water, light, sleeping place and escape plan. Activate to review the ward's limits, your recorded readiness and the next story trail. The journal neither constructs a base nor guarantees safety. A dawn observation can be recorded automatically, but is not required to continue."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Review refuge preparations"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "the Count's prison roll"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "A scratched list of prisoners, confiscated belongings and dates. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Names repeat on the execution notices. Shoes and cloaks were sorted before the sentence, as though the owner had already ceased to be a person. One entry was crossed out and replaced by 'sent below'. There is no altar here: terror was an ordinary office routine."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "the Count's physician ledger"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Linen-bound observations beside incomplete attempts to treat transformed servants. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The early pages discuss boiled linen and ordinary wounds. Later sketches show an extra mouth growing through a servant's chest. The writer stopped calling it an illness: fragments of the master's flesh were forcing a second life into the victim. His treatment could not reverse it. The servants are finite, not a renewing garrison."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Theresia's folded ribbon"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "A carefully folded cloth ribbon from the daughter's untouched room. Activate to examine. It grants no protection."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The ribbon lay beside sewing and a book kept clear of dust. A note calls the room Theresia's and orders the servants not to disturb it. The same ruler who signed the prison lists protected this little island of ordinary life. Her whereabouts are not recorded; the servants kept this door closed as the rest of the house fell apart."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "annotated routes from the residence"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "A clerk marked movements beyond the residence. Activate after defeating the Count to consult the independent hunts."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "These are separate trails: Black Dogs on one route, a mist-filled valley on another. The Count's death does not close those wounds. After the battle, consult the hunt journal to choose a destination; each place keeps its own result."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Consult the independent hunt routes now?"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "residence service key"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "A plain iron key for the barred passage between the prison offices and execution hall. Other routes stay open without it."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "residence pantry chest"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Bread, dried meat and a sealed waterskin were put aside for the household."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "searched residence chest"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The useful contents have been recovered. No new supplies will appear here."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "residence armory chest"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Worn weapons, damaged armor and a little repair material remain in the armory."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "confiscated belongings chest"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Different prisoners' clothing was sorted beside a roll of names."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "physician's linen chest"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Clean linen and one portion of thyme oil in a separate skin lie beside handwritten observations."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "prison clerk's chest"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "A service key and annotated routes lie in the records chest."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "untouched sewing box"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "This small sewing box was spared the violence elsewhere in the house."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "execution notices"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Names, sentences and orders to surrender personal belongings."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The notices call fear order. The west prison holds the lists; the kitchen passage and broken western wall offer quieter approaches than the main yard. All lead toward the stairs in the northeastern hall."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "door of an untouched room"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "A quiet family room beyond the execution hall."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The plate names Theresia. Bedding is folded, the sewing laid out, and none of the prison's chains were brought here. At the threshold, the marks of violence stop; beyond it, someone tried to keep a little ordinary life intact."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "barred service shortcut"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "A key opens the latch. A long or short sledgehammer can break it. The courtyard route is not locked."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "opened service shortcut"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The displaced grille leaves a short passage between the prison offices and the execution hall."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The service passage is open. It stays open; no key or tool is consumed."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Open the service grille with the key?"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Break the loose latch with your sledgehammer? Thirty seconds; the noise can attract enemies."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Iron rings against the stone passage."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The prison clerk kept a key; a long or short sledgehammer can also break this latch. Use the open courtyard or the kitchen route if you lack both."
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "Why is the family room untouched?"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "\"That is Theresia's room. He kept it free of what he did to the rest of us. It tells you something about him; it does not erase the execution lists. I do not know where she is now.\""
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "\"The stairs are in the northeastern execution hall. Cross the open yard, approach through the kitchen and offices, or use the break in the western wall. The clerk's key opens a short barred passage, but you do not need it. Below, the exposed seam is in a separate northern alcove; leave space around the pillars during the fight.\""
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "'Find a defensible existing building, put your sleeping place within eight tiles of a bone and stone ward, and prepare drinking water, light and a retreat. Examine the ward from indoors to record readiness in your refuge journal. It quiets only the Brand's nighttime summons; wandering enemies and the armor's shadows remain. The first hunt's recovered supplies include one finite set of ward materials. Prepare the arm cannon when you can; let your wounds rest and choose your next journey carefully.'"
msgstr ""

#: effects/refuge_eocs.json effects/count_residence_detail_eocs.json
msgid "The journal keeps your refuge preparations. Survive the Eclipse and return before following the post-Eclipse trails."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "woven campaign matting"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Layers of cloth and woven straw keep sleeping gear and stores off the trampled earth."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "rough timber screen"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Heavy upright timbers divide the cages and the fighting ground. They obstruct sight but can be broken."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "petal-strewn forest soil"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Flowers grow thickly over old footprints. Their sweetness cannot hide the smell beneath the roots."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "shallow forest gully"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A worn shallow channel runs beside the grove. Its bends offer a longer route around the cocoons."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Mistvale giant tree"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "An immense trunk rises above the grove. Silk hangs between its roots; a dark opening faces the trampled nest."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "interwoven Mistvale roots"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Thick roots and trapped stones form an opaque screen. There is room to move around either end."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "searched campaign belongings"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The useful contents have been recovered. Nothing is replenished here."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Black Dogs stolen muster roll"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A campaign roll marked with confiscated tools and missing prisoners. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The lists separate soldiers, prisoners and those taken to the leader. Human boot sizes and ration counts fill the early pages. Later marks describe warped guards wearing the same uniforms. This was an army before its cruelty took a monstrous shape. The broken wagon lies west of the tents; the quarry leaves a southern way around the cages."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Black Dogs escape testimony"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A captive left directions scratched on a folded scrap. Activate to read; no escort is required."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "I hid this before they counted us. The cage doors are tied, not locked with iron keys. Untie them from either side and pass through; the quarry is longer but stays open. The bells in the wagon can ring after you leave. Do not stand there waiting, and do not believe the leader will stop hunting because he hears them. One name at the bottom is followed by a small word: escaped."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Black Dogs command orders"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Mud-stained orders from the command tent. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Wyald ordered the stolen stores counted and the fighting ground cleared. Timber screens were dragged to its edges; three wrecked barriers remain on the open earth. Leave space beside them for a sidestep when he braces to charge. The last order names a world broken open: his old fate was diverted by the crossing, and the being leading this camp is alive, not an echo."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Mistvale searcher's testimony"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A searcher wrote down the trail of people drawn to a promise of paradise. Activate to read."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "They called the winged things fairies because the flowers were beautiful. I followed their lost shoes past the games to the silk. The still shells were empty of hope; the moving ones held something already changed. Break a swelling cocoon before it opens and no creature will fly out of that shell. I cannot bring the transformed back. The shallow western gully bends around the grove toward the great roots."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Mistvale faded ribbon"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A small ribbon caught where the games ended and the cocoons began. Activate to examine. It grants no combat bonus."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The ribbon was tied around a twig as a marker in a game. Another knot is clenched inside a split shell farther along. The flowers kept growing when the games stopped. This little thing records a person, not a treasure hidden in a creature."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "plundered baggage chest"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Rope, leather and a campaign roll survived under the broken wagon cover."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Black Dogs mess stores"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A cook put a little food and water aside beneath the tent matting."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "stolen repair chest"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Damaged campaign weapons and sewing materials were sorted for repair."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Black Dogs command chest"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Orders and a worn piece of armor remain in the leader's tent."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "prisoners' bundled belongings"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Confiscated cloth and one escape account lie inside the cages."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Mistvale travelers' bundle"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A last meal and dressings were left beside the searcher's notes at the forest edge."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Mistvale abandoned keepsake"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A faded ribbon is caught beside the abandoned playthings."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "searchers' last rest"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A waterskin and a little cloth remain by an old resting place in the gully."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "cut bonds in the cage"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A cut cord and scratches show that somebody found a way out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The cord was cut patiently, strand by strand. Muddy human footprints lead through the western cage door toward the quarry. There is no prisoner left to escort, only a route someone paid dearly to find."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "trampled Black Dogs battle approach"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Deep paired tracks end beyond the timber screens. Wide paths run along both edges."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The leader's ground lies beyond the timber. Three wrecked barriers break the open earth, with space to sidestep and strike back. The quarry on the west remains a way out; crossing the inner clearing may bring Wyald into the fight."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Mistvale trail of lost shoes"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Shoes and scraps become smaller as the trail enters the flowers."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The tracks enter a bright clearing and do not return. A searcher's bundle lies behind you. Ahead, the games give way to silk. The western gully is slower, but avoids the heart of the cocoon grove."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "split cocoon with a tied marker"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A brittle split shell holds an old knot and a searcher's mark. It contains no living captive."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Someone marked this shell before cutting it open. The cloth inside is torn through the middle, not worn out. The searcher scratched: I was too late; I can only warn the next traveler. This shell cannot be used to reverse a transformation. Around the roots, other cocoons still swell."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "silk-bound root threshold"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Flowers thin out around roots that dwarf the grove. A clear opening faces the nest."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The great tree hides Rosine's nest. Its roots and stones interrupt a straight dive, but neither route is a sealed shelter. There are only a few winged sentries. Swelling cocoons can add more; destroy a shell before it opens or keep to the gully. Beyond the threshold, Rosine may join the battle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "broken campaign barricade"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A heavy timber barrier dragged onto the fighting ground. It can break under force; the sides are clear."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "plundered wagon wreck"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "An axle and torn canvas mark a wagon stripped for loot."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Black Dogs punishment post"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Cut ropes and old marks remain on a timber post beside the training ground."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "campaign straw bedding"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Straw and worn cloth make a rough bed on the tent matting."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "tied Black Dogs cage door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A cord holds the timber door shut. Examine to untie this optional passage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "open Black Dogs cage door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The binding cord is loose. The passage remains open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Untie this cage door? The quarry route stays open without it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "You loosen the cord. This cage door is open; the other door can be untied from either side."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "wagon harness bells"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A wound cord can shake the harness bells after a delay. The mechanism can be used once."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "wound wagon harness bells"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The wound cord is running down. Three short bursts will come from this wagon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "spent wagon harness bells"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The frayed cord has broken. These bells cannot be wound again."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Wind the wagon bells? They ring in 15 seconds, then twice more. Get behind cover before they sound."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The bells are wound. The sound will come from the wagon, not from you. A guard who sees you may ignore it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Harness bells clatter at the broken wagon!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "abandoned Mistvale silk shell"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A dry, empty shell can be cut into a little usable cloth once. No creature lives inside."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "stripped Mistvale silk shell"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Only brittle strands remain after the cloth was recovered."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "swelling Mistvale cocoon"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Something flexes inside the silk. An approach may start its hatching; smash the shell before it opens to stop that creature."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "splitting Mistvale cocoon"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The silk is splitting. Its one occupant may emerge in a few seconds; destroying this shell stops the hatching."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "A nearby cocoon bulges and starts to split! Its shell can still be smashed before the creature emerges."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Broken shields, shackles and stolen clothing hang beside the training yard. Human soldiers left ration lists and rough bedding; the guards remaining here are warped followers. The prisoners scratched a way through tied cage doors. Beyond the timber screens lies the leader's fighting ground."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Tiny shoes and torn playthings lie under the flowers. The games end where the silk begins. Dry shells lie split and empty; swelling cocoons may open after your approach. Their occupants cannot be turned back into people."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "Broken orders name Wyald, leader of the Black Dogs. The crossing between worlds diverted his old fate: this is a living apostle, not an echo. His heavy rush needs a clear line. The quarry and side paths leave room to retreat; the tied cage doors offer another passage. A scratched note points toward Rosine's mist-filled valley."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "These orders call Wyald alive. How can that be?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "'The crossing did not bring every life along the same path. In his world, Wyald's fate had already been cut short. Here that thread turned aside. The camp's master is no projection; destroying him ends this hunt, but leaves the other wounds of the world open.'"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "The Mistvale searcher could not save those in the cocoons."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "'A promise of paradise can become a prison. You may stop a shell from releasing its creature, and you may keep a small memory of those lost. That is not a cure for transformation. The searcher followed those who vanished, and returned with a warning rather than the people they sought.'"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Wyald and Mistvale location details (0.I-1)
msgid "I have another question."
msgstr ""

msgid "\"Begin by refusing battles you do not need. The armor will hide pain; it cannot replace the blood you lose. Watch your body when the rage passes, and keep supplies where your remaining hand can reach them. Strength without judgment only brings the next wound sooner.\""
msgstr ""

msgid "\"Beyond the first hunt lies a sheltered grove. A witch named Flora tends the old tree there. Ask her what the Brand has done to you before pursuing a greater enemy. If you carry cursed armor already, let her see it. I can mark the road, and leave you the directions so you need not depend on finding me again.\""
msgstr ""

msgid "\"The mark is a wound between worlds. It feels what your eyes cannot yet distinguish. Pain is a warning, not a promise that the thing has found you. Seek cover, listen, and keep a way out.\""
msgstr ""

msgid "A carved arrow points west: \"Woodland road.\" The path winds between old trees and disappears behind the grove."
msgstr ""

msgid "A little floor plan labels the library, kitchen, guest rooms and workshop. The northern gallery skirts the trunk; the southern passage opens onto the herb garden."
msgstr ""

msgid "A wooden marker reads: \"Herb garden.\" Beyond the beds, a gate opens onto a footpath running south."
msgstr ""

msgid "Beyond the pale ribs, a motionless figure watches the slaughter. The air is heavy; even the creatures fall silent near him."
msgstr ""

msgid "Can I learn to stop before the armor takes over?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Count: Consult the recovered trail to locate the lair."
msgstr ""

msgid "Count: Explore the marked lair and enter its inner arena."
msgstr ""

msgid "Count: The breach is closed and the reward was already received."
msgstr ""

msgid "Count: The breach is closed. Return to its seal to collect the remaining relic."
msgstr ""

msgid "Count: The encounter has begun. Defeat the keeper or retreat to prepare."
msgstr ""

msgid "Count: The keeper is defeated. Examine the local breach and seal it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Deep tracks cut across the ground. Fresh splinters and a sharp animal smell lead into the shadow behind the broken cover."
msgstr ""

msgid "Flora: After the first hunt, ask the Skull Knight for Flora's road or consult the post-Eclipse notes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Flora: Flora is known. Talk in her peaceful house; armor and readiness are separate decisions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Flora: Flora's house has burned. The escape is complete; the attack will not restart. Recover, then choose an unfinished hunt below."
msgstr ""

msgid "Flora: The sanctuary is under attack. Escape beyond the grove by the west road or south garden."
msgstr ""

msgid "Griffith stands before you, silent and untouched by the slaughter. The sight of him drives you into a blind rage. Demons close in from every side and seize your left wrist. You hack through your own wrist to tear free as claws rake your scarred face. You stagger free, your scarred face wet with blood."
msgstr ""

msgid "Griffith stands before you, silent and untouched by the slaughter. The sight of him drives you into a blind rage. Demons close in from every side and seize your left wrist. You hack through your own wrist to tear free; a claw destroys one eye as you wrench yourself out of their grip. You stumble free, blood running down your face."
msgstr ""

msgid "Griffith stands before you, silent and untouched by the slaughter. The sight of him drives you into a blind rage. Demons close in from every side. You tear your already ruined arm free as claws rake your scarred face. You stagger free, your scarred face wet with blood."
msgstr ""

msgid "Griffith stands before you, silent and untouched by the slaughter. The sight of him drives you into a blind rage. Demons close in from every side. You wrench your already ruined left arm from their grip, but a claw destroys one eye. You stumble free, blood running down your face."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grunbeld: Consult the recovered trail to locate the lair."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grunbeld: Explore the marked lair and enter its inner arena."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grunbeld: Follow the marked road to the fortress."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grunbeld: Grunbeld is dead. The wound beneath his fortress still needs to be examined."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grunbeld: The breach is closed and the reward was already received."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grunbeld: The breach is closed. Return to its seal to collect the remaining relic."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grunbeld: The encounter has begun. Defeat the keeper or retreat to prepare."
msgstr ""

msgid "Grunbeld: The keeper is defeated. Examine the local breach and seal it."
msgstr ""

msgid "I am ready to accept the armor. What must I know?"
msgstr ""

msgid "I have the armor. Help me prepare to leave the grove."
msgstr ""

msgid "I will return when I have followed the trail. Wait here."
msgstr ""

msgid "Pressed herbs lie beside a half-mended sleeve. Root-grown shelves follow the curve of the tree. Beyond the western door a narrow woodland road leads away; to the south, garden steps descend between medicinal beds."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rosine: Consult the recovered trail to locate the lair."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rosine: Explore the marked lair and enter its inner arena."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rosine: The breach is closed and the reward was already received."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rosine: The breach is closed. Return to its seal to collect the remaining relic."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rosine: The encounter has begun. Defeat the keeper or retreat to prepare."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rosine: The keeper is defeated. Examine the local breach and seal it."
msgstr ""

msgid "THE ROAD AFTER THE ECLIPSE\n\nFirst steps: <context_val:campaign_first>\nRefuge: <context_val:campaign_refuge>\nNight: <context_val:campaign_night>\n\n<context_val:campaign_flora>\n<context_val:campaign_count>\n<context_val:campaign_wyald>\n<context_val:campaign_rosine>\n<context_val:campaign_grunbeld>\n\n<context_val:campaign_quiet>\n\nChoose your next known destination in the mission journal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tell me more about that."
msgstr ""

msgid "The log ends abruptly: \"The specimen stays in the northeastern tent until transport arrives. Nobody sleeps beside it. The southwestern alarm is on a delayed crank: turn it, then leave the clearing. A creature followed the last test sound, but attacked when it saw Mikhail. Do not let it see you.\""
msgstr ""

msgid "The standard hangs from a blackened beam. Shield rims have fused into the stone below it. Deep gouges cut through the inner gate; whoever broke this defense did not need a siege engine."
msgstr ""

msgid "The trail cannot be followed from here yet. Keep the recovered directions; try again after traveling beyond this area. Your completed hunts and known destinations remain recorded."
msgstr ""

msgid "The transport order is crossed out. Below it: \"Three of us dreamed of the same red face. We moved the case out of the sleeping tent; the scratching moved with it. At dusk, the thing at the fence turned toward the siren instead of the light. Tomorrow we leave the equipment and carry only the wounded.\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Why does it hurt before I see anything?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Wyald: Consult the recovered trail to locate the lair."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wyald: Explore the marked lair and enter its inner arena."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wyald: The breach is closed and the reward was already received."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wyald: The breach is closed. Return to its seal to collect the remaining relic."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wyald: The encounter has begun. Defeat the keeper or retreat to prepare."
msgstr ""

msgid "Wyald: The keeper is defeated. Examine the local breach and seal it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora preparation and route repair
#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Do not hurry because the armor is yours. Put your supplies in order, learn how to stop its rage, and choose your road. I can give you a charm for leaving the grove when the time comes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora preparation and route repair
#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "What remains before I can set out with the armor?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora preparation and route repair
#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "What still needs to be prepared?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora preparation and route repair
#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Preparation must take place at Flora's home by the spirit tree. Follow the directions to her grove; meeting her elsewhere is not enough."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora preparation and route repair
#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Return to Flora in the marked grove before confirming preparation. The charm protects the way out of her home."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora preparation and route repair
#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The Brand has not yet drawn you through the Eclipse. Ask Flora about the armor and return when you have survived the ritual."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora preparation and route repair
#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The armor is not ready. Ask Flora for the missing pieces, or bring your complete set or packed armor back to her. You do not need to defeat another apostle first."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora preparation and route repair
#: dialogue/flora.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Your preparation is already confirmed. Equip the armor, take what you need, and activate Flora's escape charm in the grove when you are ready. Until then, you may rest and talk."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "A hunched demon forcing its way through the broken roots. It follows the attackers into the grove, tearing at the defenders before turning on anyone left behind."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "A paper charm prepared by Flora for leaving her grove. Put on your armor and take what you need before activating it at her home. Awakening the charm is your decision to set out; there is no second confirmation. It needs no power and cannot repeat a journey already begun."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "A small sign of stone and bone quiets new night summons within eight tiles. Set your bed near it, indoors if you can. It does not turn back wandering demons or the dead already at your door. Prepare water, light and an escape route as well."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "A sword can cut a path through the boundary; it cannot mend every place where two worlds have torn one another open. I act where I can. You survived to do more than follow the next blow."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "A thick-limbed half-demon advancing behind the raiders. Ash clings to its hide as it drives the assault deeper into the grove."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "A witch tends a protected grove beyond the first hollow. Speak to Flora about the Brand and the armor before pursuing a greater enemy. The local breach is another task; neither road erases the other."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "And the armor has a price too?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "And the local breach?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Ask Flora about the Brand, the armor, and the help she can offer for your journey."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Ask what the Brand has done to you and how to endure its nights. If you carry cursed armor, let her see it. Learn its price before relying on it; counsel costs you less than another wound."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Awaken Flora's escape charm"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Behind you, fire spreads through Flora's home. You have escaped, but a shelter is being lost. Darkness is taking deeper root in the world of Cataclysm; closing every rift will demand far more than the battles won so far.\n\n<context_val:flora_next>"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Can I quiet it long enough to sleep?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Can an apostle's relic help me?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Can one of them free me from the Brand?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Carry the finished prosthetic arm cannon in your inventory and activate it there. The mount where your left hand used to be must still be empty. You need not wield the cannon or find an autodoc to attach it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Come closer to the hearth. You have brought a wound from beyond this world, and questions enough to burden any traveler. Where shall we begin?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Consult the trails already recorded in your journal. Choose one unfinished hunt, prepare for the country it crosses, and return to your refuge when wounded. Each sealed breach gives only its own surroundings a little respite."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Does that make the apostles projections?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Each trail leads to its own creature and its own wound. Finding one does not erase the others. Read the signs before choosing an enemy; the journal keeps the roads you have learned, and records which breaches remain open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Find a defensible building and leave yourself a way out. Prepare water, light and a sleeping place; a bone-and-stone ward will quiet the Brand near your bed. Replace the missing hand when you can, then follow the marked hollow. Do not seek a greater enemy while you are still recovering."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Find the witch in the marked grove. Ask about the Brand and the armor, accept the help you need, and prepare for the road before deciding to leave."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Flora offers the prepared bundles in the kitchen, workshop and southern gallery, and gives you her travel notes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Flora's counsel"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Flora's grove is the next place to seek counsel. The ashen wound is a separate road you may follow when you are prepared. Keep both directions; you do not have to answer every danger today."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Help me choose the next road."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "How can I keep its rage under control?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "How do I make that shelter useful?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "How do I tell an original from a reflection?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "I brought my own armor. What should I know?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "I brought things from those who did not escape."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "I have set aside food in the kitchen, repair materials in the workshop, and what you need for a small ward by the southern gallery. Those bundles are yours with my blessing. Take my travel notes as well; the rest of these shelves serves the household."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "I lost the charm. May I have another?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "I need to go. Wait here."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "I want to prepare for the road."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "I will finish preparing first."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Is there any armor left here?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Keep a refuge to return to. Prepare the equipment you can use with your remaining hand, and choose one unfinished trail from your journal. The wounds will not all close in a single hunt."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Learn what the armor asks of its wearer before accepting it. You may also take the help I have set aside for the journey."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Must I hold the cannon to attach it?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "No relic can restore a life sacrificed or make the Brand disappear. Carry a trophy for the help it can give, and learn its limits. A little more strength, time or shelter from heat is no reason to stand where an apostle will strike."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Not yet. I want to speak a little longer."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Prepare the charm. I understand the danger."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Recover at your refuge. Consult your journal for wounds still open and trails you have not completed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Remind me how to use the charm."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Rest, prepare your supplies and make sure you understand the armor. I can prepare a charm for the road when you are ready. The separate trails in your journal need not all be followed at once."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Show me the Count's trail."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Show me the next road."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Show me the road to Flora."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Smoke spills through the gallery. A burning bough falls across the northern rooms; the fire has reached the living quarters."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Some trophies retain a little of the power that shaped their former master. They may help you strike a demon, keep the armor's rage longer, or endure a danger you could not bear before. Wear them for their purpose, not as a promise of safety."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Something is pressing against the outer roots. I can prepare a charm to open a way out when the grove can no longer hold it back. Put on your armor and gather your supplies first. Awakening the charm means you have chosen to leave; the western path and southern garden are your ways out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Tell me about the Berserker armor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Tell me about the Brand."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Tell me about the independent hunts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Thank you. I must go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The Black Dogs' unfinished trail remains in your journal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The Count's unfinished trail remains in your journal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The armor drives the body beyond pain and fear. That is its gift, and its danger. A wound you no longer feel remains a wound. The longer you rely on its rage, the harder it becomes to judge what your body can still bear."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The ashen breach is still open. Its location remains in your journal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The charm is ready. Keep it with you while you finish gathering what you need. When you awaken it here, set out at once by the western path or the southern garden. You may still rest and speak with me until then."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The charm tightens against your palm. Beyond the northern trees, something breaks the ward. Roots rise to meet figures approaching from the east. The western path and southern garden are still open."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The collision broke more than the ground. Some lives were drawn away from the deaths that awaited them. That does not make every being here a projection. Kill a living original and that life ends; breaking a reflection leaves its source untouched."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The directions lead to a sheltered grove. Flora tends the spiritual tree there; its location is marked on your map."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The grove can no longer shelter you. Take what you learned here into the world; the remaining wounds will not close themselves."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The grove is under attack. Leave by the western path or the southern garden."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The grove is under attack. Take the western path or the southern garden and keep moving until you are clear of the trees."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The living tree quiets the Brand while the grove is protected. Beyond it, a bone-and-stone ward can quiet new night summons within eight tiles. It will not drive away a creature already hunting you. A roof, water, a bed and a way out are still worth preparing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The marked forest hollow is your first trail. A lesser apostle hunts the paths around it. Clear a way to retreat before entering the low ground; what you find there may tell you where the nearby wound lies."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The outer roots give way. Demons pour between the trees as the northern timbers catch fire. The guardians hold the approaches for a little longer."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The road to Grunbeld's stronghold remains in your journal. Follow it when you are ready."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The roots are breaking. Leave through the western path or the southern garden. Do not spend these last moments in conversation."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The tree is the heart of this house. The books are kept above the western study, the guest rooms below it. The northern gallery leads to the kitchen; the southern one reaches the workshop and garden. You may rest, read, and sit beside the hearth. Leave the household in the care you found it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "The unfinished trail to the misty valley remains in your journal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Then keep it close, and remember what we spoke of. The armor will answer your will; it will not choose wisely for you. Take time to put your supplies in order before the next journey."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Then what can one survivor change?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "What kind of shelter can quiet it?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "What road should I take next?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "What should I ask her first?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "What should I prepare for the night?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "What you carry is not merely spoil. Tell me whose memory you brought out of the dark."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Where should I go after I recover?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Who are the apostles and the God Hand?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Why can't you close these wounds yourself?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Why does the Brand hurt before I see anything?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Will the Brand let me sleep here?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "You have already entrusted the armor to me."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Your charm is ready. Equip the armor and take your supplies; activate the charm in the grove when you decide to leave."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "Your charm is ready. Finish gathering what you need, then decide when to awaken it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "demon raider"
msgid_plural "demon raiders"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. ~ Flora siege and staged counsel
#: dialogue/flora.json dialogue/skull_knight.json effects/flora_siege_eocs.json
msgid "demon reaver"
msgid_plural "demon reavers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: mods/Berserk/flora_siege_counsel_fix
msgid "This charm was prepared for a survivor of the Eclipse. It remains quiet in your hand."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/flora_siege_counsel_fix
msgid "The charm is not prepared yet. Ask Flora to help you prepare for the journey, then accept her offer. Receiving or wearing the armor alone does not awaken it."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/flora_siege_counsel_fix
msgid "These unfinished pages gather Flora's notes on paths between worlds. A smooth stone holds down the loose sheets; careful annotations crowd the margins. Beside them lies a quill she has not yet cleaned."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/flora_siege_counsel_fix
msgid "Flora's grove has fallen. You escaped with what you could carry. Recover at your refuge, then follow a trail you have not completed."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/flora_siege_counsel_fix
msgid "The road to Flora's grove is known. Ask her about the Brand and the armor, rest, and prepare for the journey when you are ready."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A cord of bones hangs beside the eastern roots. A small wooden crank winds its delayed mechanism: four bursts begin after 20 seconds and repeat every 15 seconds. It can be wound again after 90 seconds. Thick roots nearby offer cover; a creature that sees you can still choose you over the noise."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A cup has rolled under the leader's table. The beds were left made; the medical tent holds open dressings, while tied repair crates remain in the torn store. Muddy footprints lead toward the eastern break in the cordon. Nobody finished packing."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A few words written on cloth and wedged beneath a broken wooden prop. Activate it to read."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A folded warning is tied to a stake beside the southern entrance. Rain has blurred the first line, but a hurried account of the alarm test is still legible."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A prayer crossed out by someone who stayed beside the altar after the others left. Activate it to read."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A rain-marked warning left for a late-arriving member of the survey team. Activate it to read the account of the alarm test."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A split wooden prop rests on a dry ledge. An iron bar and a coil of rope were left beside it; a scrap of writing is caught beneath the end."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A wax-stained sheet has been pinned beside the altar. The final lines are written across the earlier prayer, in a different hand."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "A worn stone pillar supports the roof above the nave. Candle soot darkens the side facing the altar."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Abandoned measuring instruments and a stained cup crowd the leader's table. A field journal is pinned beneath a weight."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "An old arrow points toward the wider gallery. Deep parallel cuts cross it; farther along, a dragged line appears between the scratches. A scrap of wool is snagged behind the next stone pillar."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Arrows made by different hands overlap beside a small drawing of a wooden peg."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Black candle wax fills the joints of the altar. Torn cloth hides older carvings; a line of bloody handprints leads toward the recess behind it."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Blankets, dressings and a list of sheltered people remain in this sacristy cabinet."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Day two: the case was moved to the northeastern tent after three people reported the same face in their dreams. Day three: Pavel tested the alarm; the thing at the case followed the sound, then attacked him in the open. Day four: Lena brought the wounded to the medical tent. The final transport request is unsigned. Most of the equipment was left packed, as if departure was only minutes away."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Deep parallel scratches cross an older hand-cut arrow on the gallery stone."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "First week: water in the east store, blankets and dressings in the southern sacristy, names of the dead beside the western graves. Later entries replace meal counts with hours spent beside the red stone. The last volunteer underlined: This was meant to be a shelter."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "I marked the wide gallery to the east. Below it, the smaller passage winds around the stone mass and meets the gallery twice. We heard the chime in the western chamber before we saw what followed it. The turns hid us from its eyes. There is a braced chute near the ladder, but its peg faces deeper into the cave. I will leave another mark by the broken prop if we reach it."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Mikhail, if you reach the camp first: we moved the wounded into the southwestern tent. The alarm is outside it, beside the broken ties. During the test, the thing by the specimen left the northern tent and followed the noise. It turned on Pavel only when he stepped into the open. The crank runs slowly. There was time to get behind the canvas; he stayed beside the crank. — Lena"
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Names have been scraped from an old memorial behind the altar. Black wax fills the cuts, but the earlier promise of shelter can still be read."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Notes on herbs and protective marks lie beside unfinished repairs. The west road and southern garden are kept clear so visitors can come and go without disturbing the beds."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Roots have grown through a torn woolen wrapping. One hand still rests beside the notch where a cutting tool broke."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Roots twist above the soil like knotted ropes. They slow a crossing but leave the way open on either side."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "String marks the successive positions of the measuring instruments. Each day the circle was moved farther from the case. Beside it, a sleep log repeats the same three names and the same sketch of a red face. The last line records the alarm test and Pavel's injury."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "The first entries list names, meal portions and borrowed blankets. A later hand has written the hours of a vigil beside the red stone over the relief rota. Near the bottom, a volunteer added: We still have water in the sacristy. Please stop bringing the sick to the altar."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "The last prayer has been crossed out. Beneath it: We barred the front doors to keep the strangers away. Now the footsteps are inside. Irina took the remaining blankets through the sacristy; I could not persuade her to come back for the stone. The western wall is broken. If anyone still hears the bell, let them follow the living, not its voice."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "The letters were written on a strip torn from a sleeve: The eastern way is wide enough to carry him, but the scratches there are fresh. I left the iron bar where the prop broke. We came back around the stone chime and reached the brace from below. The peg can be pulled from that side. If he wakes, we will try the ladder before we try the red face again."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "The memorial was altered rather than broken. Names are scraped away, but the older words offering shelter remain. Wax fills the altar joints, and handprints continue around its far side. The books in the sacristy still carry the names of their donors."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "The oldest marks lead toward the red face. Later arrows point back, first cut neatly and then scratched in a hurry. One ends at a drawing of a peg. The hand beneath it wrote only: From the far side."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "The tent wall has been pulled away from its stakes. Folded canvas and snapped ties lie on the groundsheet, leaving a gap wide enough to pass through."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "The transport order is crossed out. Below it: Three of us described the same red face after sleeping here. When we moved the specimen, the scratching began outside its new tent. Pavel is hurt; the alarm test drew the creature away until he stepped out from behind the canvas. Cancel collection of the sample. Send transport for the wounded. We are leaving the equipment."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "The wrapping carries the same two-knotted cord as the ward farther up the path. Only one set of bones remains here. A shallow groove in the soil leads toward the abandoned camp, then disappears beneath new roots."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "Two deep wheel grooves end where the cart lost a wheel. Someone carried its cloth bundles to a small camp east of the track. The roots have grown over the return footprints; higher up, a two-knotted cord hangs from the bark."
msgstr ""

#: mods/Berserk/behelit_adventures_block_c
msgid "We left the cart on the old track. The face is caught in the roots, just as he said. At the eastern edge, the bones rang and the thing beneath the trunk turned toward them. I waited behind the thick roots until it passed. We will return by the old western track. If only one of us reaches the cart, leave the other name on the cord."
msgstr ""

