#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Godot sets your blade beside his tools. \"Come back in two hours. I will see to the edge and the worn metal.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Godot checks the blade. \"Still in good condition. No repair needed yet. Keep your materials.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "\"The blade needs work. Bring one steel lump and 50 charcoal, and leave it with me for two hours.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Leave this blade, one steel lump and 50 charcoal with Godot? The repair takes two hours."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Show Godot a blade"
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Godot lays your repaired blade at your feet. \"Good as new. Take it.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "\"Your blade is not beside my tools. If you took it, bring the same blade back so I can finish.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "\"Not yet. Give me two hours from when you left the blade.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "\"Leave it here this time. Another two hours; you have already paid for the materials.\""
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Return your blade to Godot"
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Close this repair order? The materials have been used and will not be returned. No blade will be replaced."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "You left a blade with me. I need two hours at the forge. If you took it away, bring the same blade back."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Show me the blade first. No sense working sound metal. If it needs repair, leave it with one steel lump and 50 charcoal. Come back in two hours."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have a look at my blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is my blade ready?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I took the blade. Here it is again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Close the repair order."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "About my blade repair."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "Godot: blade repair."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "*Blade repair. The agreed time has passed. Return to Godot at the forge to collect your blade."
msgstr ""

#. Godo blade repair
msgid "*Blade repair. Godot has the blade and the materials. Allow two hours, then return to the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Homemade early battle sword
msgid "Homemade Guts' battle sword"
msgstr ""

#. Homemade early battle sword
msgid "A roughly forged copy of Guts' broad battle sword. The uneven edge still bites deep, but the heavy blade pulls against the hand and its imperfect temper makes it prone to damage."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Still alive, I see! Is your sword in one piece?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It has been a while. Heard what is happening? Even the daylight seems darker. Something bad has happened."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Back again. What is it this time?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You left a blade here. Have you come about the repair?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am still waiting for the steel and the rest of your delivery."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your blade is at the forge. Ask me how the work is going."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your great blade has not been forgotten. What do you need?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Alive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Awake at last. Last time you crossed the threshold on your own feet. This time someone had to carry you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Easy. You have been through enough. This is my forge. I am Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot looks at your blade, then raises his eyes. \"Guts. Thought I would recognize you by that iron when I could no longer make out your face. What is it? Straighten your sword again?\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If you want a forge, you have found it. Mind what you touch. I am not fond of strangers. Rickert can show you where to rest."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*The smith turns the billet in his tongs. Only after a few hammer blows does he notice you. \"Close the door. And step away from that bucket.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Griffith... Where is that bastard?!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where is everyone?! What was that dream?!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where is my hand? Where is Rickert? What the hell happened?!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where is Rickert? What happened?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Who brought me here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How long have I been here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My belongings..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know how I can repay you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you Godot? I am looking for a smith."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I heard you can mend weapons here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I was looking for somewhere to rest."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It still serves me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a better blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good to see you, old man."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is work to discuss."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Just looking in."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us talk, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What sort of work do you take?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a good sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You found him. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Blades, iron, fittings. Show me the thing and I will tell you whether it is worth the work. Gears and little mechanisms are Rickert's business. His eyes are better than mine."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here is my blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rumors do not do my work for me. Show me. Put it on the edge of the table, away from the heat."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Understood. Thank you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is a place for a traveler. Rickert can show you. No sleeping in the workshop, and leave the tools alone."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. Then we have an understanding."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I see. A more careful owner would make it last longer. Put it here; let me look."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show me the old one first. What remains of it tells me more than your wishes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then stop standing in the doorway. You are letting in a draft."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not lie to me. Let me have a look."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Bed upstairs. You know the rest."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Calm down or you will pass out again. You have no strength left."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Easy. Rest first; we can talk when you have recovered. You can tell me what happened then."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Long enough. I do not count the hours at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First make sure you can stand. Then count your iron."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You were lying in my arms, barely breathing. What else was I to do? Not the gift I would have chosen, but here we are."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Get back on your feet first. I do not bargain with a dying man over water and a place by the wall."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I cannot tell you what you saw. I only know the wounds are real."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A knight. Tall, armored. He laid you down here and told us to prepare water. Ask him the rest; he is waiting outside."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "An armored knight brought you. Said you could recover here. He has gone on his way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your body is no excuse for what you do with your hands. Speak, and keep your quarrels away from the boy and my hearth."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Speak, Guts. The iron is cooling."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What did you want to ask?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About my order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How long have you lived at the forge?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I wanted to ask about Rickert."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is something I need to tell you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Something is changing in me. I accepted it to survive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what is happening to me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will stay here a while."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will go and find the materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come back if you have work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Until next time, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Stay. Just leave the passage clear; do not stand in the way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Go on. Check the list before you leave so you do not have to make the trip twice."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come back and we will see what is ready by then."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Go."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show me the iron and tell me what it must endure."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a reliable heavy sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a sword for fighting those creatures."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have a look at this sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have a look at this homemade copy."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I made this blade myself. What do you think?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My blade needs inspection."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "They say you once made a sword to kill a dragon."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About an order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why use different steels in a sword?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I brought ore. Will that do?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About making a new blade for me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot taps the anvil without turning. \"Another soldier full of stories. A sword is a tool. It must be balanced and quick. Too heavy, and you will die winding up for the first swing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right, forget it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need a powerful blade. It need not be that extreme."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can handle the weight. Ordinary swords break when I put all my strength into them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come back if you need something. Ask Rickert, too. He may have something useful for you. Not a sword, but useful all the same."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you take the work?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There. You can listen after all. I can try, but you will have to bring the materials. I am too old to go looking for them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Listen. A sword is forged for a person. It must be an extension of the hand. I have done this since I could hold tongs. I will not waste steel and heat on a useless monstrosity no one can fight with."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then make a blade I can use."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Think. No need to hurry before the iron is in the fire."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Put it down. Even that much iron has parts that need watching."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let me see. Has the grip turned? Does the guard press into your palm? How is the swing?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Heavy. Familiar to you, then. The edge shows it has not been idle."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It serves me well."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It needs repair."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could you improve it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I thought it was almost impossible to break."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It feels different now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then the fitting was worth the work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not without changing its shape and finding the balance all over again. That would mean making a new sword."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Anything can break. Especially if you keep testing whether it can take one more blow."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show me the grip. Then take it again. We will see whether it is the blade or you getting used to it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then keep looking after it. A sound blade deserves that much."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot turns the sword, checks the grip and draws a thumb across the edge. \"Someone took pains with this. Still a long way from a fine blade, but better than nothing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot checks the grip and the edge. \"What matters is how it behaves in the hand. You worked at it, I can see. A long way from a fine blade, but better than nothing.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You could have praised it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There was no other suitable weapon."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I wanted to learn."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Flattery makes a worse smith. Your life depends on the blade; one mistake can end it. Do not take offense."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A good reason to pick up a hammer. Live with it now. You will feel where you went wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Keep it, then. Pick it up again after a few more attempts and you will see the mistakes for yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Hmph. I did. A long time ago."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do dragons even exist?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why take such an order?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Who could use it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you consider that sword a failure?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The puffed-up fool who sent the plans never thought about that. He wanted a toy everyone would talk about. Vanity brings plenty of foolish things into the world."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "An order from above. They asked for a sword that could cut a dragon, so I forged one. I met the terms exactly. Nobody thought to ask whether an ordinary man could lift it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "None of those pampered lords could use it. That was then. You know what sort of hands it has reached now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Nobody then. Certainly none of the pampered lords who ordered it. Not a knight in the kingdom could use it. It stayed there, dead weight."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The iron was what I intended: strong and deadly. But it was useless to the people it was meant for. A smith must think about the hands that will carry his work. You have reminded me of that."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. The iron was exactly what I meant it to be: strong and deadly. It was useless to the people it was meant for. A smith must think about the hands that will carry his work. That blade waits for someone as mad as it is."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The same creatures that left those wounds on you?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A blade for fighting those creatures? Tell me why you need it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Ordinary weapons shatter against them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I want to reach whoever is behind this nightmare."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need to protect myself and those I care about."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you make me a Dragonslayer?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Creatures of the abyss are no wild beasts. If ordinary steel will not do, we must make a blade that bears the impact without dragging its owner into the grave."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before the one at the top, there are those below. You order it with rage in your eyes, but you must carry it on the days when you have no strength left to be angry."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Protection is a heavier burden than revenge. Then listen. Where will you fight? How much can you carry? What balance are you used to? I need honest answers."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I know a blade that could hew demons. That old design. I also know how much good steel and charcoal it takes. We will not finish it in an evening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what to bring. I will find it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need time to prepare."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Soft steel folds at the edge; brittle steel breaks. Heat, temper and shape must suit the work. Bring sound steel, not a promise of it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Ore has to be smelted first. For these orders, bring steel ready for the forge. Rickert can help you tell the pieces apart."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Try stores of metal, old workshops, or steel you have smelted yourself. Keep the good high-carbon pieces separate from the ordinary steel."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will return what you brought for the unfinished blade. The work is over."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before we go on, tell me what has been troubling you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is needed, what you brought, and what is left to do. That is a proper order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The battle sword order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The Dragonslayer order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the blade repair."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I lost my road journal. I need another."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Something has been weighing on you. If it concerns this work, tell me before we continue."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My answer has not changed. There will be no new blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A long battle sword, no ornaments. Bring 4 steel lumps, 1 high-steel lump, 200 charcoal and 2 leather patches, all together. Then give me twelve hours at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For this delivery: 4 steel lumps, 1 high-steel lump, 200 charcoal and 2 leather patches. Bring the whole lot so I can begin."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "In the forge. Metal does not like haste. You can see to your own equipment while I work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Finished. Come over here and take it by the grip."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "That order is settled. We have nothing more to exchange for it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You already have the blade. If you left materials for another, take them back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The materials are here. Everything you asked for."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will take the finished blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do I still need to bring?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why so long? I am short of time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I already have the blade. Return the unused materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have changed. What about our agreement?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You promised to return the materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Inspect my blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Because I will not give you a weapon with a hidden crack I could have found in the forge. Heat, hammering and cooling take their time. Want quick? Find a club in the woods. Want to live? Wait."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. The metal is here. Now it is my work. Give me twelve hours and do not hover over my shoulder."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. That part is settled. Ask what is needed next before you leave."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is needed now?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will return everything you brought. I have no use for what is not mine. Come here and take it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need to explain what happened."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First I need 32 steel lumps, in loads of eight. Then 8 high-steel lumps, 600 charcoal and 4 leather patches. After the final delivery, give me two days."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need 32 steel lumps in all. You have brought <u_val:berserk_godo_sword_iron_given>. Bring another load of eight when you can."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The ordinary steel is here. Now bring 8 high-steel lumps, 600 charcoal and 4 leather patches."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are eight steel lumps."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are the high steel, charcoal and leather."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. The metal is here. Now it is my work. Give me two days and do not hover over my shoulder."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We have settled the account. There will be no blade for this order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Finished. Take the grip. Now lift it... Careful! Do not swing; I still need that ceiling. How does it feel?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It sits well in the hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Heavier than I expected..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Remember that feeling. If the grip starts to shift, repair it before it loosens completely."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Learn its weight in an open space, not a narrow passage full of creatures. Bring the blade back into guard after each blow."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot clears a space beside the enormous black blade. \"Finished. Come around and help me shift it. A blade for things a man was never meant to fight. Your Dragonslayer.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "With this, I will finally have a chance."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will come back, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A chance, yes. It is only iron. The rest, whether you live or die, is yours to do."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come back. We will see how this iron serves against your demons."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Keep your grip. And... take care of yourself, boy."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You left me a blade. Two hours at the forge; then come and ask for it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Put it in the light. First I will inspect it. If it is sound, keep your steel. If it needs work, I need the blade, one steel lump, 50 charcoal and two hours."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the Dragonslayer..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The coals will keep. Ask."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why live so far from other people?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How long have you worked at the anvil?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You are old and ill. You could have put the hammer down long ago."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let me sit by your forge a while."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember what you told me at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here I can hear my own hammer. In town, people sometimes cannot hear their own work through all the empty talk."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do people bother you that much?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "But customers must be harder to find here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you and Rickert get lonely here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Since I could hold tongs. First I carried billets and water and worked the bellows. Then I was graciously allowed to spoil the iron myself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you spoil much good iron?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "When did you know you were a master?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I could have. Long ago."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then why keep going?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Every morning I see what I did not finish the night before. I know where my day begins. By noon a shapeless lump has become a thing someone can use. Enough to feel alive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you never want a different life?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If you understand, you have been luckier than most wanderers."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A man who knows why he came does not bother me. Being asked to admire a crest for half a day instead of making a sound weapon does."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have more than enough work. Extra gold will not make these hands younger."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert always finds a way to break the silence. Sometimes before I have had time to miss it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Enough. Some of the rubbish I made when I was young still makes me ashamed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "When I stopped blaming the steel every time a blade cracked. Steel does not lie. The smith's hand does."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I wanted plenty of things when I was young and foolish. But I always came back to this forge of my own accord."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He has learned a few things. Invented a few more while I grumbled about making simple things complicated."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What sort of things?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you approve of his inventions?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why did you let him stay here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert is taking our conversation hard."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert decided to leave the forge and travel with me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Talk to Rickert. Tell him to come with me. He will listen to you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Fastenings, triggers, little springs. I would make a thicker piece of solid steel. He spends an hour on a drawing, removes half the iron, and the damned thing still works."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If it survives a real fight, yes. If it breaks in the hand, he makes it again. Better for his hands than any praise."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The boy needed a place to live. He has lost his companions. There was room here, and another piece of bread."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The boy needed somewhere to live. There was room here and another piece of bread."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is that the only reason?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you want a longer, tearful story? If you can help the boy, you help. No need to make a speech."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I see it. His hammer falls out of rhythm; he overheats the forge. It is hard on him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He has more questions than answers. Do not make him guess what you are able to tell him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I did not know how to tell him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have not been able to tell him everything."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How should I speak to him now?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Nobody knows the right words for that. Losing people is a blow to the head, however you dress it up."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not promise some vague later if you cannot do it now. Tell him plainly: I will tell you the rest when I can. He can understand honesty."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not expect him to understand it all and move on today. Give him time. When he can speak, let him ask his questions. Answer without hiding behind excuses."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He decided that himself? Without you leaning on him?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. It was his decision."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Remember that he has a head of his own. A companion, not spare hands for your weapon or a slave to carry loot. Treat him with respect."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I understand, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not want to let him go, do you?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. Do not make me search the woods for you if a hair on his head is harmed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not. I am old and used to having the boy here. But I will not lock him inside for my own comfort. His road is his to choose."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He has given his answer. Do not go around him through me. He has his own life. If he said no, respect it. Go about your business and stop begging."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Set the iron down. I am listening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My companions died in that nightmare."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "People were dying in that nightmare. I still remember it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will find him. Whatever it costs."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Something is changing in me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Sit by the fire. We can talk."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I should have done something. Saved them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I still remember their voices."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I cannot go on talking about this now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What could you have done against that abyss?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I should have died with them!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need to be alone."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then do not pretend you knew the answer and chose cowardice. You did what a human body could do."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for listening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "But you are alive. By a miracle or by your teeth, you got out. Now you have to live with that. Living on is the hard part."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If you cannot, you cannot. No need to tear the wound open. We can sit quietly by the forge. Warm yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us sit quietly."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about one of them, if you want. Who they were before that day. Remember people alive, not torn apart."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Judeau."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Pippin."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Corkus."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Gaston."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not yet. Thank you for listening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He looked after the people beside him. Tell me about that, not just the way he died."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you. Enough for today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A man who stood between danger and his companions. That is worth remembering."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A man has more to him than a sharp tongue. What did he hope for?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A life beyond battle. Work, a place of his own. Not a foolish dream."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I believe you. If you have the strength, you will find him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is that all? You will not try to stop me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What would be the point? You did not come for my blessing. But revenge is the end of a road. When you want to talk about how to reach that day without losing your mind, I will be here at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can see what is happening to you. Your skin, your eyes... Why did you let that corruption in?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What change? Explain it properly."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I was given this power. My body is becoming something else."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I took the power from one of those creatures."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I agreed to serve those who are stronger. This is the price."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You promised to return the battle sword materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You promised to return the Dragonslayer materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I already have the sword. Will you demand it back?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "May I remain at the forge?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you understand where it will end? Iron changes in the forge too. Leave it too long and it becomes slag."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I needed the power to survive!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I still decide what I do. My mind is my own."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not want to argue, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Defeating it was not enough? You chose to become it. The abyss can poison people even after its creatures die."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Serve them? What if your master tells you to turn that weapon on the people you came to for help?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Maybe you did. Everyone wants to live. But I will not forge a sword for this new road of yours."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You agreed to help me before. Why refuse now?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then listen to my answer while you can. I will not make that blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then we will not argue. I have told you the work I will not take."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You came as a person asking for a person's weapon. Now you ask me to arm what you are becoming. I do not know that creature. I will not help it grow stronger."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you throwing me out?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is that your final answer?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I refused to forge you a blade. The rest depends on your behavior under my roof. Act like a person and you may remain."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Final."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It is yours. You fought with it; you answer for it. I will not tear it out of your hands. But if the Dragonslayer breaks, I will not take new work on it for this road."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "In a hurry? Stay a little. Hand me those long tongs."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Let me help."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Sorry, old man. Another time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "As you wish. Go about your business."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot lifts the white-hot billet from the forge. Light crosses his worn face. The hammer falls; sparks scatter across the dark earthen floor. \"What do you see before you?\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot returns to the iron. He does not resume the conversation."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Iron. Fire. Sparks."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I see your work, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Nothing special. Let us talk about something else."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I watched those sparks when I was a child. Thought that beauty was worth swinging a hammer all day. Fool that I was."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What changed?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "They let me hold the billet myself. Soon learned to watch my fingers and where I was striking, not the sparks."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is left after the fire?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then look closer. The finest-looking thing here disappears the quickest."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The sparks go out. The iron remains."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A bright spark, then nothing. But the iron remains. Each morning I can see what I did yesterday. Where I straightened it. Where I ruined the steel."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "People are more complicated than iron."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you saying I only look at the sparks?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is what remains after the fire really enough for you?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Of course. Iron is more honest. It does not try to tell me that a crack inside has done it good."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you see in me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you talking about my anger?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you think remains for me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have changed. Does it still apply to me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have not accused you of anything. I asked what you could see in the dark."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not every day. But I can return to the anvil next morning and go on with the work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You have lived from one battle to the next a long time. You know where to stand, where to strike, and how to reach the next dawn."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It is what I do best."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I see that. But what will you do with a peaceful day? One day without a fight?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will find something worth living for."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know. I never thought about it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will decide when that day comes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your anger got you out of the grave. But even here by the fire you sit as though you must spring up and run."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "While I sit here warming myself, he is out there. Alive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Perhaps. And you? Are you alive?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "As long as I can hold a weapon and fight."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If I stop for a moment, it will all come back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not understand. You were not there."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You ask whether your blade can survive the next creature. Suppose it can. What will you do when the fighting is over?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You ask whether your blade will last another fight. Suppose it does. What will you do with a day when you do not have to swing it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I want a safe place where I can just live."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There are people I need to return to."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now I just want to survive tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You chose to change your nature for strength. What will you hold on to with that changed body?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My own life. I want to protect it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can protect the people I care about with this strength."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Freedom. Nobody will dare command me now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Search hard, boy. Do not expect a purpose to appear as if by magic when you kill your last enemy."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is no shame in not knowing. At least you can begin with that admission."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Mind that the habit of killing does not decide for you before you can open your mouth."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "And when your wounded body cannot raise the blade? Will you deny yourself the right to live that day? A sword cannot replace a beating heart."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Fear is a poor companion. If the nightmares return, there is someone here who can sit beside you until they quiet down. You are not alone in these woods."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. I was not in your hell. But I can see what is happening here. I can see how carelessly you treat the little you managed to keep."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A good aim. Keep it in mind. One day you must decide what to do with your hands besides striking."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then make the journey. Try to get back before they tire of waiting or die. The road takes more time than you think."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Fair enough. Find a few minutes even in the worst day that you do not have to give wholly to fear."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Everyone wants to live. Then do not hurry to throw away everything human you had before this choice."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let them speak to you as equals. Even when they say things your new nature does not like. Do not become their monster."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Pride. Then you must answer for each step yourself. That takes more strength than empty threats."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "*Godot turns back to the anvil. \"Enough talk. The iron is cooling.\""
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let me work the bellows."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for the conversation, Godot."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I should go."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Steadily. Not too hard yet; do not burn through the coal."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Mm."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Give me back the tongs and do not get in the way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "And what have you decided?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am still thinking. It is not simple."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I think I have something to return to."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am not hurrying you. These things take time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. Then we did not sit here for nothing."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "At Godot's hearth"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Ask what you came to ask."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts. Still alive. Sit down and catch your breath."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My body is changing. Can we talk about a new blade?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will not take new work on the Dragonslayer. I can still inspect an ordinary blade."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before we discuss this blade, tell me what has been weighing on you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I accepted an inhuman power. What about my sword?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Godo dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. The iron was what I intended: strong and deadly. It was useless to the people it was meant for. A smith must think about the hands that will carry his work. A blade like that only makes sense for someone as mad as the design."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Hey. Can you hear me? It is Rickert. Take it slowly. You are back at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You are at the woodland forge. Godot lives here; he is a smith, and I help him. I am Rickert."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You are awake. Good. I am Rickert. We tended your wounds when you were brought here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You frightened me. Really. Next time, try opening your eyes a little sooner. I had time to imagine the worst."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts?.. Guts, you are awake!"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have not forgotten your bolts. Have you come about the batch?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am still waiting for the metal for your hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The first delivery is here. I still need the small fittings."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your mechanism is being looked after. Shall we discuss the work?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts! I heard steps and thought Godot was sending me for charcoal again. Have you been here long?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Oh, you are alive! How was the road? Legs intact, equipment holding up?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Shall we stop for a moment, or talk as we walk?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Careful, do not step there. A pin the size of a fingernail. I have lost it in the grass twice already... Ah. Sorry. Are you here for Godot?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Hello. I am Rickert; I help at the forge. What brings you here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts. Good to see you on your feet. What did you want to talk about?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will listen. Just give me a little room while we talk."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. I need a smith."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First I wanted to see what you are making."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am looking for somewhere to sleep."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Wait. Who brought me here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert... Thank you for helping."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Give me some time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have been here before."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember Godot, but we have not spoken."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Is it safe here?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show me what you are working on."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need help with equipment."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what happened..."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the place I came back from."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I would like to know more about you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About our road."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About your decision not to travel with me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Something is happening to me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You were not there when I came back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He is at the forge. Wait until he puts down the hammer; otherwise he will not hear a thing. I am Rickert. I help him here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does he always greet people like that?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You have not even spoken to him yet! Sometimes he barks so loudly you want to turn around. Then he takes work every other smith would refuse."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Checking the trigger. Sometimes it releases a moment late. On a table you barely notice; with the string drawn, that little fault can cost a life."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you notice the fault yourself?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Trying to make it stronger?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. At first I thought I had assembled it badly. Took it apart, put it back together: same problem. Now I am looking for the part wearing faster than the others."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now, I would settle for it firing when I pull the trigger instead of when it feels like it. The rest can wait."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is room upstairs. Tell Godot before staying, though, or he may mistake you for something worse than a traveler. Leave the tools where they are; if you need something, ask."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you live here too?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. I work. Learn. Occasionally even sleep, when Godot cannot find another urgent job."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A knight in a skull-shaped helm. He brought you here, then went on his way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A knight in a skull-shaped helm. He brought you to the door. We were too busy tending your wounds to ask him much."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am glad you woke up. Really glad."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. I am nearby if you need me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then you know the place. We only get to meet now. Not the best circumstances, but here we are."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He said he had seen you before. I mostly help with the work here. I will try to help you, too."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now, yes. It is quiet outside. We are nearby. We can talk about the rest when you feel better."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You needed help. We could give it. Do we need a better reason?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You came back... What happened to you? I was not there; I did not see. Tell me when you can. It does not have to be now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "With a crossbow I can help before the enemy reaches us. I am no swordsman. I choose a position early and try not to waste a shot; there may not be another."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What if you miss?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could it reload faster?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would you rather learn the sword?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where do you get your ideas?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "This world has things you have never seen."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Still working on that trigger?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need bolts."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then I will be glad I chose cover before firing. Looking for it with a blade at your throat is a little late."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The mechanism can change. Convenience costs weight, complexity or reliability. Make it lighter, and rain may trouble it; faster, and it may jam. I have more testing to do."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I would like to. But I will not become stronger than everyone who attacks me. Better to do what I know well than do badly what others live for."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Usually something starts annoying me. A strap rubs, a fastening takes too long to open, a part cannot be replaced on the road. Then I cannot stop thinking until I find a way to fix it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does it always work?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does Godot help?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Of course not. Sometimes fixing one problem creates a worse one. That is why I test things here, again and again. Better I break it safely than someone breaks it in battle."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "In his own way. I know more about mechanisms; he sees through the metal. I spend half a day on a clever drawing, he looks once and says, \"It will break here.\" He is almost always right."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have you brought something? Show me before I try to guess how it works."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here, take a look."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You have seen those things before. What do you think?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Sometimes I can tell what a thing does from its shape. But how they made it so small and even... I would spend a week fitting one part by hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could you reproduce it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you interested?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Some parts, perhaps. The rest I would have to learn from nothing, and I am not sure our forge has the tools. I will not promise to build an unfamiliar thing after looking once."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Very. Just bring things that are unloaded and cannot go off by themselves. I have to examine them with my hands."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Godot handles blades. I can make bolts; ask me about what you need."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Can you do something about my hand?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About bolts."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where can I rest?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is working with Godot like?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Which work did you want to discuss?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the prosthesis."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the bolts."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you still finish my order?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I promised to finish the work, and I keep my word. That does not change my decision about traveling with you. Work is one thing; the road is another."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Godot grumbles, but he lets me try. When I ruin something, he makes me explain what I did wrong. Sometimes that is harder than doing it over."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We can talk about the crossbow or another job."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How is the mounting? Does it press or chafe?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You have not fitted it yet? I can show you again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "That order is settled. If there is a problem with the device, tell me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us go over what is still needed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I think so. First I need to work out a mounting that holds without pressing on the wound. Then a mechanical hand. A small barrel can fit inside."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You want to put a cannon in it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First I just need to hold things again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will it survive a shot?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What will you need?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the mounting."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About the arm cannon."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Remind me how to fit it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I assembled this mechanism myself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I came across this device."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you still help with my hand while my body changes?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am not ready for this yet."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. One shot, then it must be loaded again by hand. There is little space. But at arm's length one shot may be enough to keep you alive."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The mounting and grip come first. If it cannot be worn all day without rubbing or falling apart, a barrel will be no use."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It needs good metal and careful fitting. I will test it before handing it over. But a charge is a charge; you still have to be careful."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Come back to it when you decide. I will not hurry you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Godot can help with the metal, but I will assemble and fit the mechanism. He thinks in blades and armor. This is smaller, finer work."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you sure you can do it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I trust you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am sure I will give it all the care I can. If it does not work, I will remake it as often as I must. You have to live with this hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You already have a mechanism. We should look after that one."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First, 8 lumps of steel and 2 pipes. After that, 2 springs, 4 leather patches and 200 charcoal. I will need six hours after the last delivery."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Right now I need 8 lumps of steel and 2 pipes. Bring them together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The steel and pipes are here. Next I need 2 springs, 4 leather patches and 200 charcoal. Do not bring the first delivery again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Finished. Let me show you the mounting first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not finished yet. The materials are here; do not worry. Go about your business for now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We have settled this order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us make it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are the steel and pipes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are the springs, leather and charcoal."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Collect the finished device."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I already have a device. Return the materials."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would Godot be better suited to this?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What is the hardest part?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Can you do this on the road?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will look for what you need."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not need a replacement hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Now everything is here. Give me six hours to assemble and test it properly."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes, this will do. I can work on the base. Bring the smaller fittings when you can."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Getting the parts out of one another's way. On a quiet table everything moves easily. Add straps, load, grit and sweat, and a generous gap is suddenly too small."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We need the forge for the heavy parts. If we travel together, we will return here to hand over the materials and collect the mechanism."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here is what you brought. Keep the device you already have."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here is where it holds to the arm. The load goes here, not on the stump. Fit it without a charge first. If it presses or moves, do not simply tighten it harder."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How do I put it on?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What about the cannon?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you, Rickert."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Take the device and start with the main mounting. You can fasten it yourself. I will show you the order of the straps so nothing twists."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Get used to the hand first. Loading and using the barrel take separate practice. Before doing anything with it, check where that barrel is pointing."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You are welcome. It may feel strange or unpleasant at first. Give yourself time; a body does not get used to it at once."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Still feels strange."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It holds well."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I want to check the device."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Start small: pick up something light, put it down, repeat. Let yourself get used to the weight before testing it in battle."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good. Still check the straps after a long road. Dust, water and strain will tell in time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Of course. The mounting, or the mechanism itself?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How should I care for it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why only one shot?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could you make another?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Keep the moving parts clean of grit and fouling. Check the mounting after every shot. If something moves differently, find out why before firing again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "There is little room and weight to spare. Another loading mechanism would take space the hand needs to grip. I chose the hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You already have one to use. If something is wrong with it, let us look at that rather than make a second for storage."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Keep grit out of the joint and watch the straps. At the forge I can repair a damaged loose mechanism: one steel lump and 50 charcoal."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show the damaged mechanism."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Wait... You assembled this without the hand? Fitting those small parts with one hand is no small task. I am impressed. I would have sworn at every step."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You understand mechanisms. Sound work. How does it behave under load?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I had to adapt."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not on the first try."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would you show me how? It could help someone else in the same position."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I believe it. Some parts are hard enough with two hands. The result matters more than how many tries it took."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let me see. First we should check whether the mounting fits you. A device made for another arm can rub you raw in an hour."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can try. I need to see how your body is changing. If the mounting stops fitting, do not force it; it could hurt you more than help."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Are you afraid of me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I still need help."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am worried. I do not know how this ends, for you or the people around you. But you are standing here asking for help. For now that is enough for me to listen."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What did you want to know about the mechanism?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It is precise metalwork. You need a forge, suitable tools and a good understanding of mechanisms. If you would rather bring materials, I can assemble it here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your ten bolts are finished. Come for them at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am working on the batch. Half an hour from the delivery; the materials are already here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I make wooden bodkin bolts with steel tips. For ten: 1 steel chunk, 1 stick, 20 thread, 10 feathers and 50 charcoal. Half an hour at the forge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Make a batch."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here is everything you need."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Collect the finished bolts."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What types can you make?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Agreed. Bring the materials and I will get to it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good, hand them over. I will check the dimensions and quality."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here are your bolts. Check how they sit in the groove before setting out; better to find a bad fit now than in battle."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Wooden shafts and pointed steel tips. The point helps, but the bow and the shot still matter."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What would you like to know? What I remember most are little things: who sat where by the fire, who always lost something and searched for it in the dark."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What were they like away from battle?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Did you fight with them?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What was Griffith like?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Judeau, Pippin, Corkus and Gaston."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you miss the camp?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what happened to the Band."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Different people. Hearing us argue, laugh and share the last bread by the fire, you would never guess we would fight shoulder to shoulder the next morning."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. I did what I could. Not everyone can cut through a battle the way you can, but there was work for all of us."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Not everyone could fight like Guts, but there was work for all of us, even me with a crossbow."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I thought I knew the answer. I thought I was following someone who led us toward something real."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I believed in him. You say the Band is gone, but I still do not know what became of him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Beside him it felt like we were going somewhere, not just surviving another battle. That is why people followed. Why I followed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you think of him now?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Now I do not know what to say. Perhaps the person he was with me was real too. Perhaps not. I do not want to guess which parts deserved my faith."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Some things, yes. Others, not a bit."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For example?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not miss the wet blanket. Or everyone remembering broken equipment a minute before marching, as if they had planned it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You still do that here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you miss?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Here I can at least say \"wait\" without chasing the marching Band with my tools."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The people. Even when they would not let me work in peace. It is quiet now. Too quiet."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what you actually know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Not all at once, though. A piece at a time, or I start drowning in it again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have you learned anything about the people who attacked the camp, or where they took Griffith?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am listening."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Guts... Where are they? What happened to everyone?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You were there. Will you tell me what you saw?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The Band was lost."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I saw what happened. Griffith gave people to those creatures."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Griffith offered them as a sacrifice. The monsters were waiting."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "People and beasts attacked them. Griffith was taken away."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I cannot talk about it now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About our friends."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About Griffith."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what comes next."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Nothing yet."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I have to correct what I told you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How many people did you lose?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Dead?.. All of them?.. Who attacked them?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I saw the ceremony. People were given to monsters. Griffith stood at its center."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Wait... Griffith? Are you saying he knew what they would do to them? Knew beforehand?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know what was in his mind. I saw what happened."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I try to picture him there, beside all that... and I cannot. He knew their names. Every one. They followed him through more than I could count."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then tell me what you saw. No more. I do not want guesses, even if they might be easier to live with."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need time. I hear you. What I remember of him does not fit your words yet. That is not your fault."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not believe me?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would you like to be alone?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for telling me. I do not know what else to say."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am not saying you are lying. I am trying to understand how the person I knew, or thought I knew, could do that. It is not the same thing."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For a little while. We will talk again. I will not hide from it forever."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I keep remembering his words, trying to understand when we stopped being people to him and became steps. A price. I have no answer."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you want to find him?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I want to hear him answer. Ask him to his face: why? What I would do after hearing it... I do not know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Today I can finish the work I started. My hands at least know what to do. Tomorrow I will try to understand the rest. One day at a time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then he might still be alive?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know what became of him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Looking for him now would be pointless."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not ask any more."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then I cannot count him among the lost yet. Not until I know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "For now, perhaps. But if you find a trace, I want to know. Straight away."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Enough for today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me as soon as you learn something. I need to know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Which part was a lie?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The attackers. And Griffith being taken. He took part in what happened."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You saw me asking about him. Hoping to find him. Clinging to that hope. And you left me with that story?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I chose what you should know. I was wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I could not say it. You should not have had to live with a lie."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would it have been easier if you kept believing?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You could have said you could not talk yet. I would have waited. Now tell me. All of it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell him everything I witnessed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You could have asked for time. I would have given it. Tell me now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I need to decide what to do with the truth myself. Do not choose what is easier for me again. You have no right."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could you trust me again?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not straight away. But you came back and told me yourself. That counts for something. We will see what you do next."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. I will not force the words out of you. Just do not tell me everything is all right if it is not."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can talk now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am still not ready."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then let us do something else for now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I cannot give an honest count. No one called the roll afterwards. They are people to me, not a tally."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what you saw. I was not there; I will not pretend to know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "They offered me strength. I refused and left as a human."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know how to put that right. But I can listen. You do not have to explain everything today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about Judeau."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He noticed when someone was struggling, and helped without making them feel foolish. You could ask him things you were ashamed not to know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I found his remains."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About what happened to him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Show the object found beside him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what you found. No comforting inventions. I want to remember the truth."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I wanted you to know."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know if it really belonged to him. Thank you for bringing it to show me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Would you like to keep it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I just wanted you to see it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. If you are ready to part with it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Give him the keepsake."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will keep it for now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about Pippin."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He said little. I would still be explaining what needed moving or holding, then see he had already done it. I felt less afraid beside him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I kept thinking he might have escaped. I was so used to him bearing more than anyone else. It seemed nothing could break him."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about Corkus."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Not always easy to get along with. One bitter remark could ruin a day. Then he would say something so absurd you could not stay angry."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I never expected to miss his grumbling. Now I try to remember his voice and cannot get it quite right."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me about Gaston."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He had plans for life after the marches. He spoke of them so often I knew them by heart. Listening, I could believe we would live like people one day."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "He spoke of the future as if it were already within reach. It is hard to accept it stayed only a conversation by a campfire."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Whom did you want to talk about?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you. I will keep it safe."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Go ahead. Just mind the cloth with the parts on it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do you ever get frightened?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "If you could choose what to work on?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does it bother you that others are stronger?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good talking with you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Of course. Especially when there is nothing left to check or tighten, my hands have no work, and my head keeps imagining the worst."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you do then?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It does not always show."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I try not to be entirely alone with it. We do not even have to talk. Sometimes someone sitting nearby is enough."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I work with my hands. From outside, being busy may look like being calm. They are not always the same."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I would still make things. Things that make living easier, not only surviving."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Weapons help people survive too."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "A mounting you can work with after an injury. A cart you do not have to drag out of every rut. Even a lock that does not jam in the cold."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. That is why I make them. Sometimes I want to make something for after the battle, too."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Sometimes. Especially when someone is trapped and I cannot move what fell on them. You stand there, hands shaking, unable to help."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How do you deal with it?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I learn what I can. Try to find a way to help before things become that bad, while there is still time to prevent it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. I have decided. We can talk about work, but not traveling together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Where are you going? And what do you expect of me if I agree?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We would help each other. I do not want to go alone."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I could use your knowledge. The choice is yours."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know yet. Let us talk later."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You will do as I say. I do not need an assistant who argues."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Come with me, or you will regret it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Your friends were weak. Be useful to me and perhaps you will outlive them."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About your decision."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can shoot, watch the equipment, help on the road. But if we are walking toward pointless death, I will say so."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will listen."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We can argue. We will decide together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I said you will obey."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am glad you say that. But I do not want to come only to mend equipment while you decide everything else. My word has to mean something."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am asking you to be a companion."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I understand. Think about it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I feed you for your help. You will obey."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then tell me where you want to go first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "First, supplies and a safe road."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "To the lair we know. We will scout the approaches first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before setting out, let us discuss what is happening to me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before we set out, tell me what is happening to you. I need to know what to expect beside you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. I will come. Let me gather my things and tell Godot; I do not want him wondering where I went."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will tell you about the change."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I changed my mind. We will stay for now."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. Better to agree now than sort it out on the road when it is too late to turn back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will be ready soon. I will not keep you long."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us discuss equipment and travel arrangements."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then you need someone else. I will not go with you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You can order work from me. You cannot buy me. That ends the talk about traveling together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. After those words, I am not going anywhere with you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not speak of them that way. Do not imagine I would walk beside someone who can say that."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I was wrong to speak to you that way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Will you at least finish my order?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for saying so. But I have not changed my decision."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How are you holding up?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What do you think of our road?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About our equipment."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I just wanted to know how you are."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am hurt. Let us find somewhere quiet and look at the wounds before going farther."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I am holding up. When we can, I want to check the crossbow without rushing. On the road I keep worrying about something I missed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I would like to know where we are going. If it is just looking for supplies, say so. That is worthwhile too."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Supplies first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We have a lead to a lair."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Before we get closer, let us look for a way to retreat if things go wrong. I am happier seeing a way back before I need it."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Ah... I see. Not always well, honestly. Thank you for asking. Not everyone notices the difference."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Want to talk?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We could just sit a while."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Something ordinary first, though, not the hardest things at once."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Were you going to tell me what is happening to you? Or was I meant to guess?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Tell me what you know about this change."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. I accepted the power."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I did not know how to start."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "It is none of your business."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know what I will become."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You do not need to understand. Just obey."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then tell me what you were promised. And what you understand yourself, beyond somebody else's words."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I accepted strength. I will not treat people as possessions."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I still need help with my hand."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Start with what you know for certain. We can work through the rest as we go."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "When we walk side by side, it concerns me too. I need to know what to expect, so I can survive beside you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You can keep your own counsel. But before I travel with you, I need to know what to expect."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Then do not hide changes from me. Tell me before it is too late. I cannot promise to stop it, but I want to understand you while I still can."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We can keep talking. My choice about the road is still mine."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us discuss the road as companions."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "No. That was not our agreement when I chose to come with you."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Can you still hold a tool comfortably with that hand?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Does that plate get in the way when you bend? You seem to move differently."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will walk behind you in narrow passages. I do not want to get in the way if you have to turn or spread those wings."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Have you noticed my hands?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The shell has changed how I move."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "The wings make things cramped."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "All right. I will be here."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Until next time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good luck. Bring them and we will carry on."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Yes. Thank you for staying with me."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "So was I. We can talk without something being broken first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "So was I. Visit without broken equipment sometimes. Give me a rest from other people's repairs."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Enough for today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We have not introduced ourselves yet."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Rickert, by the way. And your name?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Introduce yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Good to meet you. Mind the parts on the cloth."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Still busy with your crossbow?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You would not believe how much time one lousy part the size of a fingernail can eat."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Take up a sword. Fewer parts: iron and an edge."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I can barely lift your sword off the table. I will keep my little parts. Safer that way."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I hear you. What I remember of him does not fit your words yet. I need time."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Could I assemble the mechanism myself?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "When we can, I want to check the crossbow without rushing. On the road I keep worrying about something I missed."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Why did you take me in?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I think so. First a mounting that holds without pressing on the wound. Then the mechanical hand and the small barrel inside."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I understand what you mean."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I will remember that."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We will follow the lead we know and scout the approaches first."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "We will look around before going farther."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About trusting me after my lie."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "My hand has grown back. What about my order?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You no longer need a replacement hand. I still have the materials you brought; you can take them back."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "You no longer need a replacement hand. Let us close that order."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Close the order and collect any materials delivered."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I remember the lie. But I have had time to listen to you since then. We can talk about the road again."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "After what came out, I need time. I can work beside you at the forge. Trusting you with my life on the road is another matter."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "What can I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Let us talk honestly about what I saw and what I mean to do."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "About traveling together."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Do not try to mend this with another fine promise. Keep speaking honestly until I can see it is a habit."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "Thank you for sitting down and telling me plainly. I cannot forget everything at once. Let us leave it there for today."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "I do not know you well enough to leave everything and go with you. Come back and talk; we will see how things go."
msgstr ""

#. Approved Rickert dialogue 2026-10-21
msgid "How can I rebuild your trust?"
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your flesh grows thick and heavy. Gain +3 strength and 3 points of natural protection. You remain slower, and gas can still hurt you. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The thickened body cannot fit ordinary rigid torso and leg armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your heavy, pliant body grants +3 strength and 3 points of natural protection. Your slower movement remains. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible. It does not heal wounds.\n\nClothing: The swollen torso and arms cannot fit ordinary rigid armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent pliant body grants +1 strength and 2 points of natural protection, with another -5 speed. Returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The thickened torso cannot fit ordinary rigid armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Dark wings lighten your movements. Gain +2 strength, +1 dexterity, +10 speed and 2 points of natural protection; falling damage is halved. The wings do not allow sustained flight. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The wings need an open back; ordinary torso clothing gets in their way."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent fiery carapace grants +3 strength, 6 points of natural protection, -15 speed and 50% less heat damage. Hunger and slow recovery remain. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible. It does not heal wounds or make fire harmless.\n\nClothing: The carapace cannot fit beneath ordinary rigid torso or limb armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent carapace grants +1 strength, 3 points of natural protection and 25% less heat damage, with another -8 speed. Returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The carapace cannot fit beneath ordinary rigid torso or arm armor."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanently grown insectlike wings grant +2 dexterity, +15 speed and half falling damage. Wings permit gliding with a light load and usable arms, not free ascent into the sky. Torso encumbrance above 20 prevents your wing abilities. Your fragile flesh remains. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The wings need an open back; ordinary torso clothing gets in their way."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent insectlike body grants +1 dexterity and +8 speed. Its fragility and difficulties with speech and crafting remain. Returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The insectlike head and hands do not fit ordinary rigid helmets, masks or gloves."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanently altered flesh grants +4 strength, +1 dexterity, +15% melee damage and 4 points of natural protection. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible. Its growth does not heal wounds.\n\nClothing: Rigid sleeves and gauntlets cannot follow the reshaped flesh."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your outline becomes difficult to follow. Gain +2 dexterity and reduce your visibility range by 3 tiles. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: Ordinary rigid helmets and masks do not fit the altered head."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "A fragile, elongated shape sharpens perception of distance. Gain +2 dexterity, +1 dodge and 1 point of natural protection. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: Elongated fingers do not fit ordinary rigid gloves."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your beastlike body grants +3 strength, +15% melee damage and -2 dexterity. Your stamina still recovers slowly. This body is permanent; returning to human shape is impossible. It does not heal wounds.\n\nClothing: The changed hands and feet cannot fit ordinary rigid gloves and footwear."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your permanent beastlike body grants +2 strength and -2 dexterity. Returning to human shape is impossible.\n\nClothing: The changed hands cannot fit ordinary rigid gloves."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Bone presses through the scar. Tendons tighten, fingers uncurl: your left hand has grown back."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "A mechanical cannon attached to the left forearm. Deploy it to wield and reload its single chamber, then retract it to use another weapon. It burns powder charges instead of bionic power."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your hand has grown back. Speak with Rickert at the forge to settle the unnecessary prosthesis order and collect any materials already delivered."
msgstr ""

#. Apostol body rules 2026-10-21
msgid "Your hand has grown back. You no longer need a replacement."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You are on your feet, swordsman. After that night, that is no small thing."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You can stand again. Then the time I won for you that night was not wasted."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Was there something else you wanted to ask?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I will hear your questions."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Was it you who carried me out?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I want to understand what happened."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Tell me about the Brand and those who come at night."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will you help me?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Where should I look for this evil now?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found something among the remains."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Who are you?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "It is time for me to go."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "That is enough for now. I will speak to you again."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found an opening and carried you through before it closed. But carrying a body out of a place of sacrifice does not free it from the sacrifice itself."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Yes. You were among those who were not meant to leave that ceremony alive. I carried you out. The people where you woke did the rest."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I carried you somewhere I could leave you safely. We did not reach the woodland forge."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Because of this mark?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Griffith. What became of him?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What happened to me?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Who are these people?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What do I need to know first?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Was saving your life not help enough?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Godot and Rickert. You have already spoken with both of them. They sheltered you when I brought you here."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You know Godot. The young craftsman at his forge is Rickert; you have yet to meet him yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Godot is a smith. Rickert works beside him on crossbows and mechanisms. You will have to meet them for yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You saw the boundary where greatness is bought with other lives. Those who rose above the crowd accepted that harvest. Those feasting beneath the throne merely did what they had been permitted."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Were those creatures once human?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "And those who stood above them?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Why is this happening among our cities?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Can things be put back as they were?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What became of Griffith?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Can the one who presided over this do it again?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Many were. They rejected their nature when an earthly existence was no longer enough. Their old failings and desires remained. Sometimes those human habits make the monsters recognizable. And vulnerable."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Can they be destroyed?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Their altered flesh can be destroyed. Do not mistake their bodies for true immortality. Nor should you look for human mercy where the abyss rules."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "How do I fight them with ordinary weapons?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Wait before you step forward. Study how the enemy moves, what it protects and when it must pause for breath. Know where you will retreat. Blind fury is no substitute for a way back."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The God Hand. Do not confuse them with the servants admitted to the feast. Killing an ordinary apostle does not bring their overthrow a step closer."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then resistance is pointless?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I defeated his reflection. How could he be there again?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "If I thought your struggle useless, I would not have carried you out of that hell."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "This land had already been wounded by its own end of the world. Another darkness seeps through the open wounds. The boundary has thinned, making your home accessible to hungrier predators."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The past cannot be restored, even if every passage is sealed. But you can keep the next traveler from meeting the same fate."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "He took the throne offered to him. Your memories of the man cannot explain the abyss into which he was reborn."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I do not care what he became. I will reach his throat."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then first learn to live until the next dawn. Otherwise your oath of vengeance will be no more than the last words of a man dying in the night."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Do not expect what you witnessed to be the last expression of that will. Your concern now is to endure the threat already following you."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You dispersed a reflection. It could take his shape and carry some of his power, but it was not the being you seek."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then that fight meant nothing?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "How can I distinguish a reflection from the original?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will there be more reflections?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The shape that stood before you will threaten no one else. That matters. But do not credit your victory with something it did not accomplish."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "A face is not enough. Consider where it came from, what holds it here and what it leaves behind. A vanished shadow is not proof of an original death."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "While the boundaries between worlds remain broken, I would not call that encounter the last."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The Brand remains a mark of sacrifice. Beings beyond the boundary can discern it where a human eye sees nothing. Night makes their journey to you easier."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Does it warn me of danger?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will they come every night?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What should I do before dark?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "How can I protect my refuge?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will closing a breach remove the Brand?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Pain and blood may come before a creature appears, especially a powerful one. Heed that warning, but do not expect it to name your enemy or show a safe road. The Brand is no friend to you. It simply is."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Not every night is the same. Sometimes you will hear only footsteps beyond a wall. Sometimes you will have to abandon your shelter and run. Silence does not mean they have forgotten you."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Find a place you can leave. Do not corner yourself for the imagined safety of walls. Prepare light, dressings and weapons. Keep what you need close: there will be no time to pack when you must flee."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will a locked door help?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will they disappear in the morning?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Against some of them, yes. But an ordinary wall cannot keep out everything that comes from the darkness. Some creatures need no door."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Dawn may end the pursuit itself. It does not promise to destroy those that already reached you. Look at what remains outside before opening the door."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "There are signs that hinder their approach. I will leave you the instructions. But a sign cannot replace shelter: choose somewhere you can defend and leave."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You have already begun preparing. Wise. But do not mistake that sign for a fortress wall. It will not destroy a creature already beside you; it hinders the way here."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then I can sleep peacefully?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Tell me how to arrange it."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "More peacefully. Not carelessly. Even a protected place must have an exit. Never make the sign your last hope."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Arrange eight stones and four bones into a sign on clear ground. Keep it close to your sleeping place. Its protection stays on the same level; it will not drive away creatures already here."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "No. You will close one road into this world, and that matters to those who live nearby. The mark on your body belongs to another bond. Closing a breach does not break it."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The trail leads to the forest hollow. The direction is already in your records. Prepare before following it; I will not choose your next step for you."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Victory left you more than a dead enemy. Examine what remains in its lair. You may find why it came to these lands."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You have found the trail of a passage. Now deal with the wound itself. A fallen keeper does not always mean the road behind it has closed."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The roads you learned are already marked. Follow an unfinished trail when you are ready. You need not take on every enemy at once."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You have exhausted the trails you had. Revisit the evidence and speak with those you trust. The next road remains to be discovered; I will not point you toward something I do not know."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "First let your wounds close. Speak with the craftsmen, gather what you need and prepare for night. The road will not disappear while you learn to walk it without falling at the first step."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found judeau's traces. I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found evidence about judeau."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Judeau saw other people even when everything around him was turning them into prey."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found pippin's traces. I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found evidence about pippin."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Sometimes a man knows he cannot hold the enemy. Still he stands between it and those who can escape."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found corkus's traces. I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found evidence about corkus."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "A victim has a life that cannot fit inside the word victim. Desires, failings, arguments. Do not give the monsters that part of him as well."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found gaston's traces. I remember him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I found evidence about gaston."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Such hopes are easily lost behind banners and the names of commanders. To him that future mattered no less than another man's dream of a kingdom."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Tell me what you found."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "It was not enough."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Not enough to stop all that happened. But you do not know how much time his act gave someone else."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I want him remembered."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then preserve more than how he died. Preserve who he was."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You call that victory?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I call it an act that cannot be measured only by who remained standing."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I should have been beside him."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You may carry that thought all your life. It cannot put you beside him that night. Decide whom you will stand beside now."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "We often disagreed."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Grief does not require that you agreed on everything in life."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "He was no hero."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "They did not need to become heroes to deserve their lives."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "That makes it harder."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Yes. You see not only a death but everything that can never follow it."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What should I do with the keepsake?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Keep it, give it to someone who knew him, or leave it in a worthy place. Memory does not demand you always carry its weight."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "One who has long walked against them."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "That is no name."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Why did you save me?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Why did you not save the others?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Were you once human too?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Can fate be changed?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Why will you not stay?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "No. But for now it tells you more than a name."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I had the chance to intervene. I took it."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "And you want nothing in return?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I did not carry you out of one bargain to immediately bind you to another."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Because I could not."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "But you knew what was happening."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I cannot accept that."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Knowing of a disaster and having the power to stop it are not the same."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I am not asking you to accept it. But do not base your next step on the belief that someone could have fixed everything with a single blow."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Enough humanity remains in me to remember what I fight against."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "And the rest?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Not every story needs to be told at another man's threshold."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "You are alive and asking that question. Begin there."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then everything depends on my choice?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "No. But your choice still belongs to you. Do not give it away merely because you cannot rule everything else."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I have my own road. Our enemies will not wait for you to recover."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Will we meet again?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Perhaps. But do not build your life around waiting for me."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Have you finished?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then know this: I will continue my journey. If you still have questions, ask them now. Do not expect me to return to this threshold."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Wait. I have more questions."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Remind me of the essentials."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I understand. Farewell."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Prepare for night. Ask the craftsmen for what you lack. Then follow a trail you know. Do not try to settle your whole war in a single battle."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Recover before another fight. Prepare what you need, and follow a trail you already know."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Farewell."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Then preserve the life with which you intend to continue."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Live on. What kind of life it will be is yours to decide."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Watch the rider leave."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Words recorded after speaking with the Skull Knight."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Close the record."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "What else did you want to ask?"
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "The Knight carried me out of the sacrifice. Escape did not undo its consequences."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Godot works on blades; Rickert works on crossbows and mechanisms. A road marker is not a personal acquaintance."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "A bone and stone sign hinders the Brand's night summons nearby. It does not remove creatures already here and does not replace shelter."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Recover before a fight. Directions are kept as ordinary missions and map markers; the road journal is only a reference."
msgstr ""

#. Direct mission routes 2026-10-22
msgid "The wound cools and its heartbeat stops. This place is quieter. The defenders' surviving marks reveal three trails: the Count's residence, the Black Dogs' camp and a misty valley."
msgstr ""

#. Direct mission routes 2026-10-22
msgid "Notes about known places, the smiths' work and what you have learned. It is a reference: your missions and map markers remain if this book is lost."
msgstr ""

#. Direct mission routes 2026-10-22
msgid "A new objective is marked on your map."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Godot works on blades; Rickert works on crossbows and mechanisms at the woodland forge."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "Recover before a fight. Prepare for night, then follow a trail you know. Do not take on every enemy at once."
msgstr ""

#. Skull Knight 2026-10-22
msgid "I wanted to ask about someone else who died."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лесная кузница"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В лесной глуши работает кузнец Годо. Говорят, он берётся за тяжёлые клинки и оружие, от которого отказываются другие мастера. Вместе с ним живёт молодой мастер, знакомый с арбалетами и механизмами."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Годо держит кузницу вдали от городов. Он знает, для чего нужен клинок, и не любит тратить железо на украшения. Если моё оружие ещё можно спасти, он скажет об этом прямо."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В лесу стоит дом с кузницей. Кто здесь работает, я ещё не узнал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Внизу находится кузница с горном и рабочим местом. Наверху — жилое помещение. Это дом мастеров, а не заброшенный склад."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Мне разрешили воспользоваться местом для отдыха. Проходы нужно оставлять свободными, инструменты хозяев — на своих местах."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "После Затмения Рыцарь принёс меня сюда. Я пришёл в себя под этой крышей."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Кузница пострадала. Прежнее укрытие нельзя считать безопасным, пока я не осмотрю то, что осталось."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "К списку"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Закрыть журнал"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дуб со сплетёнными корнями"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В глубине леса стоит огромный дуб. Переплетённые корни скрывают землю у ствола."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Между корнями искали камень с человеческими чертами. Люди, оставившие этот след, считали находку достаточно важной, чтобы вернуться за ней."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Корни разбивают землю на тесные проходы. Следы чужой работы обрываются среди свежих зарубок. Прежде чем подходить к стволу, стоит осмотреть путь назад."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Камень оказался настоящим. Я забрал его из-под корней."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пещера отголосков"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Под землёй расходятся широкие галереи и тесные боковые ходы. В темноте трудно судить, насколько далеко уходит пещера."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Разведчик оставил сведения о лестнице, обходе и старой подпорке. По его следу здесь искали камень с человеческим лицом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Звон каменной подвески слышен за поворотами. Существо в глубине реагирует на него. Звук может выиграть время, если путь к лестнице подготовлен заранее."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Узкий ход соединяется с галереей. Подпорка мешает проходу; добраться до её крепления можно со стороны глубины пещеры."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Бехелит найден среди подземных следов. Выбираться отсюда всё равно придётся обычным путём."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лагерь пропавшей экспедиции"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Среди леса оставлен лагерь с палатками и снаряжением людей этого мира."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Экспедиция изучала необычную находку. В записях повторяются сны о красном лице. После переноса образца возле палаток появилось существо."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Раненых переносили в отдельную палатку. Дозорный советовал держаться укрытий и не пересекать открытое место перед существом. Последний приказ требовал вывезти людей, оставив снаряжение."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Образцом был Бехелит. Экспедиция успела понять опасность слишком поздно."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лесная часовня"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В лесу стоит часовня. Старая дорога приводит к её дверям."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Здесь принимали путников и раненых. Позже обитатели перенесли за алтарь необычный камень и начали считать его чудом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Двери закрыли перед теми, кто искал помощи. Шёпот приняли за ответ на молитву. Следы у алтаря говорят о том, чем закончилось ожидание чуда."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "У часовни есть обходной путь. Последние записи советуют искать живых, а не возвращаться за камнем."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Камень из реликвария оказался Бехелитом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лесная низина"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "След исчезнувших путников ведёт в лесную низину. Здесь скрывается существо, которое охотится на людей. Перед спуском стоит осмотреть подходы и оставить путь для отступления."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Существо погибло. Среди его останков могут сохраниться следы тех мест, откуда оно пришло."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В найденном клочке описаны разрушенный фундамент и расселина в земле. След ведёт к отдельному прорыву."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пепельный разрыв"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Среди разрушенных оснований открылась рана в земле. По краям лежит пепел, из глубины доносится тяжёлый пульс. Это отдельный проход между мирами."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Хранитель пал, но пульс не прекратился. Сам проход ещё нужно осмотреть."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рана остыла, её пульс затих. Здесь стало тише. Существа, уже прошедшие в этот мир, никуда не исчезли."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Среди уцелевших отметок различимы пути к резиденции Графа, лагерю Чёрных Псов и туманной долине."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Клеймо осталось со мной."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Закрытие прохода не изменило то, что происходит с моим телом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Укреплённая резиденция"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Резиденция Графа"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "След привёл к укреплённому дому. Известные сведения называют его резиденцией Графа."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Укреплённый дом за внешней оградой. Кто распоряжается им, я ещё не узнал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "За внешним порядком скрываются казни, заключение и слуги, чьи тела уже нельзя назвать человеческими."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Один из пленников рассказал о знакомых ему помещениях и служебном проходе. Его сведения касаются этого дома; о происходящем за его пределами он знает немного."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Граф погиб. Власть хозяина над этим домом закончилась, но связанные с ним следы ещё требуют внимания."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Проход при резиденции закрыт. Для окрестностей это передышка, а не конец вторжения."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я принял покровительство Графа. Вместе с новой плотью пришло место при его дворе. Что он называет защитой, ещё предстоит испытать на себе."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Военный лагерь"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лагерь Чёрных Псов"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "След ведёт к лагерю Чёрных Псов. В полученных сведениях назван их командир — Уайлд."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Среди леса разбит военный лагерь. Я ещё не узнал, кому подчиняются его обитатели."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Здесь пересчитывают добычу, держат пленных и исполняют приказы командира."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Военные порядки сохранились даже среди чудовищ. Людей записывали рядом с пайками и снаряжением, словно всё было частью одной ведомости."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Уайлд погиб. Его смерть не отменяет того, что происходило в лагере, но теперь этот хозяин больше никого не уведёт к себе."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я согласился войти в Чёрных Псов. Уайлд обещал силу и жизнь без человеческих запретов. Моё тело изменилось сразу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Туманная долина"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дорога ведёт в туманную долину. В полученных сведениях её связывают с именем Розины."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дорога привела в туманную долину. Кто скрывается среди её обитателей, я ещё не узнал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Над цветами кружат существа, которых называли феями. Следы исчезнувших людей ведут к шёлку и огромным корням. Красота этого места ещё ничего не говорит о его обитателях."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В коконах меняются тела. Разрушить оболочку до её раскрытия — не то же самое, что спасти того, кто когда-то оказался внутри."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Розина погибла. Обещанное ею убежище больше не примет новых жертв по её воле. Судьбу уже изменённых людей одной победой не вернуть."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я принял предложение Розины остаться среди её обитателей. Новое тело появилось сразу. Человеческая речь стала труднее, а обещанное чувство безопасности не заменило собственной воли."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Крепость"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Крепость Грюнбельда"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Полученные сведения связывают крепость с Грюнбельдом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Мощные укрепления закрывают внутренний двор. Чей приказ здесь исполняют, я ещё не узнал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "У духовного дерева Грюнбельд остался жив. Этот след может привести к новой встрече с ним."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Грюнбельд погиб у духовного дерева. В крепости остаются последствия его власти и связанный с ней проход."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "После боя у духовного дерева я потерял его из виду. Этого недостаточно, чтобы считать его погибшим."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Грюнбельд пал. Перемена облика продолжила его сопротивление, но теперь бой действительно окончен."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Проход в крепости закрыт. Окрестности получили передышку."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я принял клятву перед Грюнбельдом. Он дал мне панцирь и место среди своих воинов. Вместе с защитой пришли требования службы."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дом у огромного дерева"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дом у духовного дерева"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Полученный след ведёт к дому у огромного дерева. В этих сведениях названа ведьма Флора."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Жилой дом соединён с огромными корнями. Его хозяйка мне пока не представилась."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Жилые комнаты соединены с огромными корнями. Здесь есть место для чтения, работы и отдыха. Укрытие держится не только на силе дерева, но и на заботе хозяйки."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора разрешила мне отдохнуть и взять приготовленные припасы. Остальные вещи дома принадлежат его обитателям."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора знает о доспехе, который позволяет телу продолжать бой ценой самого владельца."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дом атакован. Прежняя защита больше не удерживает всех врагов. Известные проходы теперь нужны для выхода."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я выбрался из дома. Позади оставались огонь и бой. Что уцелело, пока неизвестно."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дом у духовного дерева потерян. Огонь прошёл через знакомые комнаты. Это место больше не может быть прежним убежищем."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Моё пристанище"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я выбрал место, куда можно вернуться с дороги. Здесь должны оставаться вода, перевязки и свободный путь к выходу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Неподалёку от места для сна сложен знак из камней и костей. Он сдерживает ночной зов Клейма поблизости, но не останавливает существ, которые уже пришли."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Прежнее пристанище больше не годится для отдыха. Потребуется найти другое место."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Годо"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Годо — хозяин лесной кузницы. Говорит резко и быстро переходит к делу. Сначала хочет увидеть оружие, а уже потом слушать просьбы о нём."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Годо узнал меня. По-прежнему ворчит на мои клинки и не бережёт слов. О железе он судит увереннее, чем другие — о людях."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Его дело — клинки, железные детали и ремонт. Механизмы и арбалеты он оставляет Рикерту."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Он принял меня, когда я не мог сам пройти через порог. Плату за воду и место у стены требовать не стал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "У горна Годо говорил об огне и искрах. Яркая вспышка быстро гаснет; работа и те, о ком заботишься, остаются. Важна не одна сила, с которой наносишь удар, но и жизнь, к которой собираешься вернуться."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я не стал слушать его разговор у горна."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Годо отказался делать для меня этот клинок. Он знает о принятой мной силе и считает, что дальше я должен отвечать за свой выбор."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рикерт"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рикерт работает рядом с Годо. Разбирается в арбалетах, спусках и креплениях. Может долго возиться с маленькой деталью, если от неё зависит надёжность оружия."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Он путешествовал с Отрядом Сокола. В бою рассчитывает на арбалет, позицию и подготовку больше, чем на силу удара мечом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рикерт помогал мне после спасения. О том, что было внутри Затмения, он не знал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я рассказал ему, что видел в Затмении. Он услышал о предательстве Гриффита и гибели товарищей."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я сказал Рикерту, что отряд погиб от нападения людей и зверей. О предательстве Гриффита я умолчал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я пока не рассказал ему о пережитом. Он остался с вопросами о судьбе товарищей."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я признался, что прежде солгал. Теперь Рикерт знает правду и помнит мой обман. Одного признания недостаточно, чтобы всё стало как раньше."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Между нами снова стало возможно доверие. Прежний разговор от этого не исчез из памяти."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рикерт решил идти со мной. Он согласился быть товарищем, а не чьей-то собственностью."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "После моих слов Рикерт отказался идти со мной. Обычная работа в кузнице осталась отдельным делом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рыцарь-Череп"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Всадник в шлеме, похожем на череп. Он нашёл проход из места жертвоприношения и вынес меня наружу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Он сказал, что имел возможность вмешаться и воспользовался ею. Нового долга за спасённую жизнь не потребовал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Он давно сражается с существами за гранью. Своего имени и прошлого не назвал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рыцарь продолжил свой путь. Он предупреждал, что ждать его у этого порога больше не следует."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора — ведьма, живущая у духовного дерева. Говорит спокойно и не обещает избавления от любой беды. Знания для неё связаны с заботой о живых."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Она объяснила, что Клеймо связывает отмеченного с иной стороной мира. Простая победа над одним чудовищем этой связи не разрывает."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора знает цену доспеха Берсерка. Он способен заставить тело продолжать бой, когда обычный человек уже не мог бы стоять."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Она позволила взять приготовленную помощь. Это дар хозяйки, а не разрешение опустошить весь дом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора услышала о моей перемене. Она не обещала вернуть прежнее тело. Разговор о том, как распорядиться оставшейся волей, оказался важнее обещания лёгкого исцеления."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пленник резиденции"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Человек, которого держали в резиденции Графа. Он знает привычки слуг и часть служебных помещений. Боится хозяина и не уверен, что помощь извне вообще возможна."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Он рассказал, что мог, о пути через дом. Его помощь позволила лучше понять, где можно обойти слуг."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Власть Графа над ним закончилась. Что он сделает с этой свободой, пока неизвестно."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Работа лесной кузницы"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "За работу здесь берут пригодный металл и другие нужные материалы. Годо занимается клинками, Рикерт — механизмами и болтами. Договорённость стоит обсудить прежде, чем приносить случайный лом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Материалы передаются тому мастеру, который взялся за дело. Готовая работа требует времени. Когда она закончена, за ней нужно вернуться в кузницу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Ремонт клинка"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Целый клинок Годо не станет перековывать без нужды. Сначала осмотрит лезвие и скажет, нужна ли работа. Если повреждения серьёзные, потребуются материалы и время у горна."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Для ремонта придётся оставить сам клинок. Пока он у мастера, в дороге понадобится другое оружие. После окончания работы я получу обратно свой клинок."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Большие клинки"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Длинный боевой клинок без украшений. Такой меч требует надёжной закалки и хорошего равновесия. Размер сам по себе не делает работу хорошей."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Мой самодельный клинок повторяет общий замысел, но он тяжелее, грубее и хуже выдерживает работу. Это моя попытка, а не изделие Годо."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Годо создал клинок для невозможной задачи — убить дракона. Обычному воину трудно даже поднять это железо. Мастер не рассказывает о нём как о красивом оружии для парада."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Протез и рука-пушка"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рикерт может собрать механическую замену потерянной кисти. В устройстве совмещены подвижная часть и скрытая пушка. Для работы нужны не только железо, но и точные крепления."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Устройство готово, но ещё не стало частью моей руки. Прежде чем рассчитывать на него в бою, нужно закрепить его и проверить работу механизма."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Протез закреплён на руке. Теперь нужно привыкнуть к его весу и движению, а пушку содержать в рабочем состоянии и заряжать подходящими зарядами."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Этот механизм я собрал сам."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я собрал его уже после потери кисти. Рикерт отдельно отметил эту работу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Арбалет и болты"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рикерт ценит надёжный спуск больше эффектной переделки. Арбалет помогает держать расстояние, но требует подходящей позиции и времени на перезарядку."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "У него можно заказать болты, передав нужные материалы. Обсуждение болтов не обязывает заказывать протез или звать Рикерта в дорогу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Камень с человеческим лицом"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Маленький камень с человеческими чертами. Его трудно принять за обычную безделушку."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В рассказах людей, которые держали его прежде, повторяются шёпот и ощущение чужого зова."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Теперь я тоже слышал этот зов. Он обращается к желанию, которое трудно произнести вслух."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Осквернённый Бехелит"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Кровь изменила камень. Зов стал настойчивее. Он обещает иной выход из церемонии, но не возвращение к прежней жизни."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я был предупреждён: переход опасен даже для того, кто откажется от предложенной силы. Изменения могут остаться навсегда."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Затмение"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я прошёл через место жертвоприношения. Отряд, с которым я знал жизнь до этой ночи, оказался среди обречённых. Гриффит стоял по другую сторону случившегося."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "По ту сторону прохода оказалось место жертвоприношения. Среди существ лежали люди и следы последнего сопротивления. Их прошлое не было моим, но увиденное уже стало частью моей жизни."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рыцарь-Череп вынес меня наружу. Церемония осталась позади; её последствия — со мной."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В той ночи я потерял левую кисть."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В той ночи я потерял глаз."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Мне удалось разрушить удерживавший сцену облик. Это не было уничтожением всей Руки Бога."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Церемониальный круг"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В конце пути меня ждали пять фигур. Они говорили о судьбе, желаниях и выборе. Предложенный дар не обещал сохранить прежнее тело."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я мог принять дар, но не назначить себе тот облик, который он даст."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я согласился. Участники церемонии вернули меня наружу. Теперь перемена продолжается во мне."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я отказался и после последнего предупреждения. Меня вернули без дара. Человеческое тело вынесло этот переход не без последствий."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Те, кто стоял у круга"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Войд говорил о причинности и решении, которое нельзя отменить. Камень привёл меня к возможности выбора, но не сделал последствия этого выбора чужой ответственностью."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Слан говорила о желании жить и о теле, которое способно принять больше человеческого. В её обещаниях плоть и страсть звучали как одна цена."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Убик обращался к памяти и к тому, как легко человек объясняет себе собственное желание. Его слова заставляли сомневаться не только в увиденном, но и в собственных оправданиях."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Конрад говорил мало. В его ответах человеческая уязвимость выглядела частью неизбежного распада. Уйти из этого места без последствий он не обещал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Фемто говорил так, словно прежняя человеческая мера уже не имела значения. Предложенная им сила не делала принимающего равным тому, кто её предлагал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "След отказа"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я вернулся человеком. Отказ не оставил мне принятой силы, но церемония всё равно изменила то, как я слышу, вижу или переживаю окружающее."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Некоторые звуки стали глуше. Чтобы расслышать знакомое, приходится прислушиваться."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Зрение уже не такое, каким было до перехода."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В точном движении появилась дрожь, которой прежде не было."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Воспоминания возвращаются без приглашения. Иногда настоящее на мгновение теряет перед ними силу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Ощущение опасности остаётся даже там, где я пока ничего не вижу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Клеймо жертвы"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Клеймо осталось знаком жертвы. Существа за гранью различают его там, где человеческий глаз ничего не видит. Ночь облегчает им путь к отмеченному."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Боль и кровь могут предупредить о близости существа. Предупреждение не называет врага и не показывает безопасную дорогу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Закрытие одного прохода не разрывает связь Клейма."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Ночные преследователи"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Тишина не означает, что след потерян. Стоит готовить место для ночлега до темноты и держать нужные вещи рядом с выходом."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дверь помогает не против всякого существа. Защита стен не должна оставлять меня без пути отступления."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рассвет не уничтожает существ, которые уже пришли. Перед выходом нужно смотреть, кто остался снаружи."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Знак из камня и костей"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Небольшой знак из камней и костей сдерживает ночной зов Клейма поблизости. Он не уничтожает существ и не заменяет стены, воду и путь к выходу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Для знака нужны восемь камней и четыре кости. Его складывают на свободной земле рядом с местом для сна."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Держать постель нужно рядом со знаком и на том же этаже. Знак действует и под открытым небом, но от этого открытая поляна не становится надёжным укрытием."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Раны между мирами"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Граница между мирами повреждена. Через отдельные проходы приходят существа, которые прежде не принадлежали этим землям."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Победа над существом, удерживающим проход, не всегда закрывает саму рану. После боя нужно осмотреть то, что оно оставило."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Закрытый проход даёт передышку окрестностям. Уже пришедшие существа остаются, а дальние раны продолжают существовать."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Отражения"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Не всякий знакомый облик принадлежит самому существу. У границ миров возникают отражения, несущие часть чужой силы."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Побеждённое мной отражение Гриффита не было его оригиналом. Исчезновение облика не доказывает смерть того, чей образ он принял."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Найденный камень оказался настоящим, хотя существо вокруг него было отражением."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Джудо"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Среди следов последнего боя я узнал Джудо. Даже там он пытался дать другим время. Помнить о нём стоит не только по этой последней ночи."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я нашёл свидетельство о Джудо. Следы говорят, что он пытался помочь другим выбраться из давки. До этой ночи у него была жизнь, о которой я знаю лишь обрывки."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "От его ножа сохранилась рукоять."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рыцарь сказал: сохранить память — значит помнить не только смерть человека, но и то, каким он был."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пиппин"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пиппин держал проход до конца. За тем местом, где он стоял, ещё могли уйти другие."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Следы у тела Пиппина говорят о сопротивлении в тесном проходе. Он остался между существами и теми, кто ещё пытался выбраться."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Среди обломков сохранилась сломанная застёжка."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Не всякий поступок можно измерить тем, кто остался стоять после боя."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Коркус"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Коркус хотел выбраться из войны и грязи. Мы часто не ладили, но это не уменьшает того, что у него отняли."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В свидетельстве о Коркусе остались обычные человеческие надежды. Чудовища оборвали их так же, как мечты тех, кого называют героями."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "От его вещей сохранился обломок ножен."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Для права на жизнь не требуется стать героем."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Гастон"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Гастон хотел однажды оставить войну и жить собственным трудом. Его будущее было тише чужих мечтаний о королевстве, но значило для него не меньше."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я нашёл след человека по имени Гастон. Он надеялся на обычную жизнь после войны. Среди огромных имён и знамён такие надежды легко потерять."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Его швейные принадлежности напоминают о жизни, к которой он хотел вернуться."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Доспех Берсерка"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Этот доспех позволяет продолжать бой за пределом обычной боли. Он не делает тело невредимым и не отменяет цену уже полученных ран."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Получить доспех — ещё не значит научиться ему противостоять. Сила, которая удерживает тело в бою, может уничтожить его владельца."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Полный доспех уже у меня. Мне нужны понимание и контроль, а не второй комплект."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "У меня есть часть доспеха. Это ещё не полный комплект."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора отказалась передать мне новый доспех после моего выбора. Она знает о принятой мной силе."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Огонь у духовного дерева"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я выбрался, но дом у духовного дерева потерян. За знакомыми дверями остались комнаты, в которых ещё недавно можно было отдыхать и разговаривать."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Закрытые раны дали местную передышку. Они не остановили столкновение миров. Дорога продолжается среди тех последствий, которые ещё можно изменить."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "След ведёт к крепости Грюнбельда."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Грюнбельд погиб. В крепости остаётся связанный с ним проход и последствия его власти."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я не знаю, что стало с Грюнбельдом после боя."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Передышка"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Те раны, по следу которых я прошёл, закрыты. В этих местах стало тише. Это не конец тьмы, но люди получили время, которого прежде у них не было."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Клеймо осталось. Следующая ночь всё ещё требует подготовки."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Принятая мной сила осталась со мной. Законченная охота не возвращает прежнего тела."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я остался человеком и несу последствия того перехода."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Моё тело"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Согласие уже дано. Я чувствую перемену, но ещё не знаю, каким станет её завершение. Возвращаться за новой долей силы мне не предлагали."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Перемена продолжается сама. Новые ощущения и потребности появляются не сразу. То, что тело выдерживает больше, не означает, что оно перестало получать раны."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я принял внутрь плоть побеждённого существа. Она не осталась обычной пищей. Теперь её сила меняет моё тело."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Назад этот выбор не ведёт. Принять другую плоть вместо первой — не значит отменить уже случившееся."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Под рубцом проступила кость, натянулись сухожилия и распрямились пальцы. Левая кисть отросла вновь. Это произошло вместе с принятой переменой, а не от обычного заживления."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Механизм пушки остался на предплечье. Новая кисть не уничтожила уже закреплённое устройство."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Тело вытянулось, пальцы изменились. Расстояние иногда ощущается не тем, каким кажется глазу. Короткий шаг способен провести меня через промежуток, который раньше пришлось бы преодолевать иначе."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Изгиб пространства может ослабить удар, но сама плоть не стала неуязвимой. Обычные жёсткие перчатки больше не подходят к рукам."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Плоть стала сильнее и подвижнее. Из неё можно вытянуть оружие, которого прежде не было. Возвращать себе силы удаётся ценой голода и времени."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Жёсткое снаряжение на руках мешает изменённому телу. Способность восстановиться не позволяет забыть о ранах и пище."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Собственный силуэт стал труднее удержать взглядом. Чужое внимание можно увести к ложной цели, а восприятие врага — сбить на короткое время."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Это не обещает власти над каждым разумом. Изменённой голове не подходят обычные жёсткие шлемы и маски."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Плоть стала толще и тяжелее. Прикосновение разъедает живое тело, а выдох оставляет едкую взвесь. Собственная сила требует осторожности рядом с теми, кого я не хочу ранить."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я двигаюсь медленнее. Обычная жёсткая броня корпуса и ног не подходит новому телу. Облако не становится безопасным только потому, что его выпустил я."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Тёмные крылья изменили спину и равновесие тела. Движение стало стремительнее. Давлением можно оттолкнуть противника и нарушить его наступление."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Крыльям нужно место. Обычная одежда на корпусе мешает им; бесконечного полёта эта сила не дала."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Тело стало тяжёлым и пластичным. Изменённая плоть выдерживает больше, а её отросток способен достать врага на расстоянии удара."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "За прочность приходится платить медлительностью. Жёсткая броня тесна корпусу и рукам. Восстановление остаётся потребностью тела, а не доказательством бессмертия."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Новое тело тянется к рывку и хватке. Ближний бой стал естественнее, точная работа — труднее."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "После усилия силы возвращаются медленнее. Изменённые кисти и стопы не подходят для обычных жёстких перчаток и обуви."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Насекомоподобные крылья раскрылись за спиной. Они помогают быстро перемещаться и смягчать падение, если тело и груз позволяют ими пользоваться."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я не стал свободно подниматься в небо. Тяжёлое и тесное снаряжение мешает крыльям, а хрупкость тела не исчезла."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "На теле сомкнулся тяжёлый панцирь. Жар стал переноситься легче, а выдох способен обернуться пламенем."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Тело требует больше пищи и медленнее отходит от усилия. Жёсткая броня не помещается поверх панциря. Сопротивление жару не делает любой огонь безопасным."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Граф назвал меня своим. Тело стало плотнее и медленнее, из него вырос отросток. Новая защита связана с тем, кто её дал."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Изменённый корпус не помещается в обычную жёсткую броню. Я принял место при чужом дворе; распоряжаться собственными поступками всё равно придётся самому."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Уайлд дал мне звериное тело. Оно тянется вперёд, к короткому броску и удару. За грубую силу приходится платить неловкостью в точной работе."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Жёсткие перчатки не подходят изменённым кистям. Его одобрение не заменяет отдыха после боя."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Розина приняла меня среди своих. Голова и кисти изменились; слова стали даваться тяжелее. Я всё ещё могу выбирать и действовать."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Прежняя человеческая работа требует больше усилий. Обычные жёсткие шлемы, маски и перчатки не подходят этому телу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Принятая клятва оставила на теле панцирь. Он удерживает часть ударов и жара, но делает движения тяжелее."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Корпусу и рукам тесно в обычной жёсткой броне. Под защитой хозяина остаются требования службы."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Связь с хозяином больше не даёт прежней поддержки. Изменённое тело осталось. Нарушенная клятва не вернула меня человеком."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Хозяин погиб. Вместе с ним закончилась поддержка, но принятая от него плоть не исчезла."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Перестройка завершилась. Тело обрело свой новый облик. Теперь мне предстоит жить с ним, а не ждать, что ещё одна ночь вернёт прежнего меня."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Печать рассечённой плоти"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Тяжёлая печать, оставшаяся после Графа. Надетая печать помогает поражать существ из-за грани. Её сила не обращена против любого живого тела."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Узел Зверя"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Жилистый узел обостряет чувство того, что движется во тьме. С ним ночная дорога различима лучше."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Покров Туманной долины"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Тонкий покров сохранил след странной долины. Надетый покров помогает уйти от удара, но не обещает спастись от каждого нападения."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Осколок пламенного панциря"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Осколок принадлежит самому апостолу. Надетый осколок помогает переносить жар, но не защищает от дыма и не делает огонь безопасным."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Его нельзя спутать с обгоревшими застёжками людей гарнизона."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Заказ с разграбленного обоза"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Колесо сломалось до сумерек. Железные крепления оставили под окованным коробом, зерно унесли."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Между страницами вложен заказ: «Отнести погнутые клинки в лесную кузницу Годо. С ним работает молодой мастер арбалетов. Держаться старых тележных троп через лес»."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "На полях отмечены повороты и переправы."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Запись разведчика"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "За открытой поляной следят. Я видел, как деревья двигались в безветрие. Привязал ранец над промоиной и пошёл нижней тропой — проверить другой берег. Если не вернусь, держитесь камня и оставляйте место, чтобы повернуть назад."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Письмо дорожной стоянки"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Уходим до следующих сумерек. Вода чистая; тем, кто пойдёт следом, одеяло может понадобиться больше, чем нам."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Кузнец Годо починил наш сломанный клинок. Его молодой помощник делает арбалетные болты. Здесь записали обратную дорогу: старая тропа, переправа через ручей, затем путь углежогов. Идти долго, но в конце дороги есть мастер."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дорожные советы Флоры"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Чистую ткань для перевязок нужно кипятить. Бурдюк лучше сшить до дальней дороги. Питьевая вода, место для сна и свободный выход важнее удобства комнаты."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Небольшой знак из камня и костей помогает сдерживать ночной зов, но не прогоняет существо, которое уже стоит у двери."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Спасённая рукопись"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора сравнивает соединённые миры с корнями, сросшимися поперёк раны. Тихое место может укрыть путника; одно убежище не исцелит весь мир."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "На полях сохранились следы дыма. Большая часть исследования осталась за оборванными страницами."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Закладка в форме листа"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Деревянная закладка в форме листа уцелела в каменной нише между корнями. На ней вырезано: «Оставь свет следующему путнику»."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Обгоревший клочок"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Между обгоревшими краями различимы оборванная дорога, разрушенный фундамент и отметки вокруг расселины. Существо из низины носило этот путь к другому прорыву."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Сломанный корнерез"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Свежие зарубки обрываются посреди корней. На древке вырезаны два ряда отметок; один внезапно заканчивается. Эти люди пытались прорубить путь к каменному лицу, а не сразиться с тем, что жило под ним."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Оберег двух путников"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Надпись называет двух путников и просит, чтобы оба вернулись домой. Второй узел завязан дрожавшей рукой. На коре рядом — такое же тёмное пятно, как на брошенном корнерезе."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Последняя записка у дуба"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Мы оставили телегу на старой тропе. Лицо застряло в корнях, как он и говорил. Пока существо обходило ствол, я ждал за толстыми корнями и не двигался."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Назад пойдём по старой западной тропе. Если лишь один из нас доберётся до телеги, оставь имя другого на шнуре."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Травник Флоры"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Травы сушить отдельно. Чистую ткань для ран прокипятить. Старые рукава починить до следующего пути. Оба прохода вокруг духовного дерева держать свободными."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Убежище остаётся убежищем, потому что кто-то заботится о нём."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Схема пещерного разведчика"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я отметил широкую галерею на востоке. Под ней тесный ход огибает каменную толщу и дважды соединяется с галереей. В западном зале мы услышали подвеску раньше, чем увидели то, что пошло на её звук. Повороты скрыли нас от его глаз."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Возле лестницы есть проход с подпоркой, но колышек обращён в глубину пещеры. Если дойдём, оставлю ещё одну отметку у сломанной опоры."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Список помощи в часовне"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Воду хранили в восточной комнате, одеяла и перевязку — в ризнице. В ранней записи упомянут путник с починенным мечом и болтами: «Кузница Годо ещё работает в лесу. Старик и молодой помощник берут за работу пригодный металл». На обороте он нарисовал дорогу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Позднее вместо порций еды стали считать часы у красного камня. Последний доброволец написал: «Это должно было быть убежищем»."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Признание хранителя"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Мы назвали камень чудом, потому что нуждались в чуде. Перенесли его за алтарь и перестали открывать дверь чужакам. Когда начался шёпот, мы решили, что нам ответили."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Отпечатки рук на алтаре оставили не во время молитвы."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лесная дорога беженца"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Если часовня потеряна, уходите через пролом в западной стене. Старая колея глубже в лесу приводит к огромному дубу с переплетёнными корнями. Путники рассказывали о другом каменном лице. Я не видел его сам."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Отмена вывоза образца"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Приказ на вывоз перечёркнут."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Трое из нас после ночёвки здесь описали одно и то же красное лицо. Когда мы перенесли образец, за новой палаткой началось царапанье. Павел ранен: существо настигло его, когда он вышел на открытое место. Отменить сбор образца. Прислать транспорт для раненых. Снаряжение оставляем."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Последние слова на ткани"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Мы ломали щиты, чтобы построить стену. Держали проход, пока не пронесли раненых. Дороги назад нет. Не теряйте бледную тропу из виду. Огромные рёбра склоняются к месту сборища."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Список узников"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Имена повторяются на объявлениях о казнях. Обувь и плащи рассортировали ещё до приговора, словно владелец уже перестал быть человеком. Одну запись зачеркнули и заменили словами «отправлен вниз»."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "За каждым ровным столбцом стоял человек, которого здесь заранее сочли вещью."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Записки лекаря"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Первые страницы посвящены кипячённому полотну и обычным ранам. Затем появляются зарисовки второго рта, растущего из груди слуги."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Автор перестал называть это болезнью. Частицы плоти хозяина внедряли в жертву другую жизнь. Привычное лечение не возвращало человека."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лента Терезии"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лента лежала рядом с шитьём и книгой, которую очищали от пыли. Записка называет комнату комнатой Терезии и запрещает слугам её тревожить."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Тот же правитель, который подписывал тюремные списки, оберегал этот островок обычной жизни. Где дочь сейчас, не сказано."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Две дороги из резиденции"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "На карте отмечены две дороги. На одной — лагерь Чёрных Псов и имя Уайлда; на другой — туманная долина и имя Розины. По краю тянутся записи о пропавших обозах и закрытых дорогах."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Списки Чёрных Псов"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В списках отдельно указаны солдаты, пленники и те, кого увели к командиру. Первые страницы заполнены размерами сапог и пайками. Позже появляются пометки об искривлённых стражах в той же форме."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "За привычной военной ведомостью проступает другая жизнь лагеря."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Свидетельство о побеге"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Я спрятал это до переклички. Дверцы клеток перевязаны, а не заперты железными ключами. Развяжи их с любой стороны и проходи; путь через карьер длиннее, но открыт."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рядом с одним именем внизу дописано короткое слово: «сбежал»."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Приказы командира"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Уайлд приказал пересчитать награбленные припасы и расчистить площадку для боя. Деревянные заслоны оттащили к краям. Между строчек о добыче и людях повторяется одно требование: никто не должен уйти без его разрешения."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Последний лист говорит о расколотом мире. Переход изменил прежнюю судьбу командира. В этом лагере живёт он сам, а не его отражение."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Свидетельство искателя долины"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Они называли крылатых тварей феями, потому что цветы были прекрасны. Я шёл по следу брошенной обуви, мимо игр — к шёлку."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "В тихих оболочках не осталось надежды; в движущихся было нечто уже изменившееся. Вернуть их я не могу. По западному оврагу можно обойти рощу и выйти к огромным корням."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Выцветшая лента"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Ленту повязали на ветку как метку для игры. Дальше такой же узел зажат в расколотой оболочке. Цветы продолжили расти, когда игры оборвались."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "От человека иногда остаётся вещь, которую легко пройти мимо."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Послание дозорного"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Михаил, если первым доберёшься до лагеря: мы перенесли раненых в юго-западную палатку. Существо вышло из северной палатки и настигло Павла на открытом месте. Держись за полотном палаток и уходи через разрыв восточного ограждения. Мы уходим до сумерек."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лена."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Последнее бдение"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Последняя молитва перечёркнута."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Мы заперли парадные двери, чтобы не впускать чужаков. Теперь шаги слышны внутри. Ирина вынесла оставшиеся одеяла через ризницу; я не смог уговорить её вернуться за камнем. Западная стена проломлена. Идите за живыми, пока ещё есть время."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Записка на рукаве"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Восточный ход достаточно широк, чтобы нести его, но царапины там свежие. Железный лом я оставил у сломанной опоры. Мы вернулись вокруг каменной подвески и подошли к подпорке снизу. С той стороны колышек можно вытащить."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Если он очнётся, сначала попробуем добраться до лестницы, а не до красного лица."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Застёжка гарнизонного знамени"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "От знамени гарнизона осталась обгоревшая застёжка. На обороте выцарапаны имена людей, державших южную дорогу."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Это человеческая вещь. Пламенный панцирь апостола не принадлежал тем, чьи имена здесь остались."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "&Дорожный журнал\n\nДороги, лица и события. То, что удалось узнать и сохранить в памяти."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "&Дорожный журнал\n\nНа этих страницах пока нет записей."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Известные места"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Люди и ремесло"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пережитое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лесная кузница — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дуб со сплетёнными корнями — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пещера отголосков — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лагерь пропавшей экспедиции — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лесная часовня — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лесная низина — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пепельный разрыв — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Резиденция Графа — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Укреплённая резиденция — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Лагерь Чёрных Псов — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Военный лагерь — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Туманная долина — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Крепость Грюнбельда — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Крепость — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дом у духовного дерева — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Дом у огромного дерева — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Моё пристанище — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "К разделам"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "&Известные места\n\nМеста, о которых удалось узнать."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Годо — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рикерт — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Рыцарь-Череп — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Флора — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Пленник резиденции — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Работа лесной кузницы — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Ремонт клинка — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Большие клинки — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Протез и рука-пушка — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Арбалет и болты — Новое"
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "&Люди и ремесло\n\nЛюди и их дело."
msgstr ""

#. Approved reference book 2026-10-22
msgid "Камень с человеческим лицом — Новое"
msgstr ""

